WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:04.820
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.120
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:07.400
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.660
And we're best friends.
我们现在是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.480
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正为你们带来终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:19.460
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.600
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.540
Hello, everyone.
大家好。

9
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:26.420
Hi.
嗨。

10
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.660
It's the finale part one.
这是大结局的第一部分。

11
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:30.600
Five years.
五年了。

12
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.600
I'm already emotional.
我已经开始感慨了。

13
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.480
Five years we've been doing this.
我们做这个节目已经五年了。

14
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:34.880
Yeah.
是啊。

15
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:35.980
And here we are.
我们终于走到这一步了。

16
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.800
The second-to-last episode of The Rewatch.
这是重温节目的倒数第二集。

17
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:46.260
Season 9, episode 26, written by Greg Daniels, directed by Ken Kuapis.
第九季第26集，由格雷格·丹尼尔斯编剧，肯·夸皮斯执导。

18
00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:58.620
Before I give a summary and get into these fast facts, we have to share what we walked into today, courtesy of our party planning committee, Sam and Cassie.
在总结剧情和进入快问快答环节之前，我们必须分享一下今天进门时看到的惊喜，这多亏了我们的派对策划委员会成员萨姆和卡西。

19
00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.540
Sam and Cassie.
萨姆和卡西。

20
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.180
I love you guys so much.
我太爱你们了。

21
00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:01.840
We got here.
我们刚到这儿。

22
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:07.240
There is a streamer entrance as you come into the studio that we had to walk through.
进录音室的时候，我们得穿过一个彩带入口。

23
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.480
There are balloons that spell out congrats.
还有拼成“祝贺”字样的气球。

24
00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.320
There's beautiful roses and a package.
有漂亮的玫瑰花和一个包裹。

25
00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:14.640
Something's wrapped up here.
这儿有个包好的东西。

26
00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:15.200
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

27
00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:19.080
There is a sign on the table that says, it is your milestone.
桌上有个牌子写着：这是你们的里程碑。

28
00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.160
And there's some scotch and Splenda.
还有苏格兰威士忌和代糖。

29
00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.540
Well played.
干得漂亮。

30
00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.480
We love you guys.
我们爱你们。

31
00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:25.480
That's so great.
太棒了。

32
00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.740
What is this package, Sam?
萨姆，这是什么包裹？

33
00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:28.540
This is from you?
这是你给的吗？

34
00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.600
That is from me, Cassie.
那是卡西给我的。

35
00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:30.120
You have one, too.
你也有一个。

36
00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:31.020
Aw.
噢。

37
00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:31.540
Wait.
等等。

38
00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:32.900
Should we open it at the same time?
我们要同时打开吗？

39
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:33.260
Yes.
好。

40
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:33.820
Okay, wait.
好，等等。

41
00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:34.400
Ready?
准备好了吗？

42
00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:35.960
I love you guys.
我爱你们。

43
00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.260
Oh, Sam.
噢，萨姆。

44
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.680
I haven't even opened it yet.
我还没打开呢。

45
00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:42.800
Already just making me tear.
就已经让我热泪盈眶了。

46
00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:43.900
What is it?
这是什么？

47
00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:44.400
Wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等。

48
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:44.480
What?
什么？

49
00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.960
It's amazing.
太棒了。

50
00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.860
This is amazing.
这真是太棒了。

51
00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.500
It's us with Keanu.
是我们和基努的合影。

52
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:54.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

53
00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.680
It's the four of us with Keanu.
是我们四个人和基努的合影。

54
00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:57.260
It's a sketch, though.
不过这是张素描。

55
00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:57.800
It's a sketch.
是张素描。

56
00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.820
It's like, how did you have this made?
就像是，你是怎么让人画出来的？

57
00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.560
It was drawn by a guy who does some of my tattoos.
是一个帮我纹身的人画的。

58
00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.620
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

59
00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.960
It's so cool.
太酷了。

60
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.320
It is so cool.
真的太酷了。

61
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.120
This might make me cool with my kids.
这可能会让我在孩子们面前变得很酷。

62
00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.220
Sam, what is the name of your friend who drew this?
萨姆，画这幅画的朋友叫什么名字？

63
00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.420
Christopher is his name.
他叫克里斯托弗。

64
00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.840
Well, we will be sharing because this is amazing.
好吧，我们会分享出来的，因为这太棒了。

65
00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.140
This is epic.
这太史诗级了。

66
00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:19.760
Epic.
史诗级。

67
00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.200
Congrats on five years, guys.
祝贺你们五周年快乐，伙计们。

68
00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.440
Thank you, Sam.
谢谢你，萨姆。

69
00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:24.880
Thank you, guys.
谢谢你们。

70
00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:29.620
And thank you for the flowers and for everything and just who you are to us.
也谢谢你们送的花，谢谢你们所做的一切，以及你们对我们而言的意义。

71
00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.480
And, oh, man.
噢，天哪。

72
00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:32.980
Yeah.
是啊。

73
00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:33.580
Yeah.
是啊。

74
00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.440
Get the tissue box out, lady.
把纸巾盒拿出来，女士。

75
00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.240
Get the tissue box.
把纸巾盒拿出来。

76
00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:36.840
Is it?
是吗？

77
00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:37.320
Where is it?
它在哪儿？

78
00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:38.400
It needs to be on the table.
它应该在桌子上的。

79
00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:39.560
It's not even in here.
这里面根本没有。

80
00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.220
Oh, wait.
噢，等等。

81
00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:40.760
Here it is.
在这儿呢。

82
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.440
It needs to be refrigerated.
它需要冷藏。

83
00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:46.200
Okay.
好的。

84
00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.780
And I'll bring it out during our break, and then we can share about it.
我会在休息时把它拿出来，然后我们可以一起分享。

85
00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:50.120
Okay.
好的。

86
00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:50.620
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

87
00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.660
Well, listen, I brought a summary.
听着，我带了一份摘要。

88
00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:53.680
Do you want to hear it?
你们想听吗？

89
00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.840
I love your summaries.
我喜欢你的摘要。

90
00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.940
Five years, and I love your summaries.
五年了，我依然喜欢你的摘要。

91
00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.660
Never stop giving me a summary, lady.
永远别停止给我做摘要，女士。

92
00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:02.840
Here it is.
在这儿。

93
00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:09.100
A year has passed since the documentary aired, and Dwight is catching us up on the many changes
纪录片播出已经一年了，德怀特正在向我们介绍这段时间发生的许多变化，

94
00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:14.980
that have occurred, Dwight and Angela will have their respective bachelor and bachelorette parties
德怀特和安吉拉将分别为他们的即将到来的婚礼举办单身派对，

95
00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:20.480
in anticipation of their upcoming wedding, and some old friends return for a documentary
一些老朋友也会回来参加纪录片的

96
00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:21.540
reunion panel.
重聚座谈会。

97
00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:28.460
Pam takes a lot of heat from the public, and Erin is reunited with someone she's been waiting
帕姆承受了来自公众的很大压力，艾琳也终于和她等待

98
00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.980
a long time to meet.
已久的人重逢了。

99
00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:31.880
All right.
好吧。

100
00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.440
Fast fact number one.
速览事实第一条。

101
00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.720
This episode aired on May 16th, 2013.
这一集是在2013年5月16日播出的。

102
00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:40.020
I looked it up.
我查过了。

103
00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.700
The pilot episode aired on March 24th, 2005.
试播集是在2005年3月24日播出的。

104
00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:50.120
So nine seasons of The Office aired over an eight-year time period.
所以《办公室》九季的播出跨度是八年。

105
00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:57.240
The script for the finale was 75 pages long with a 40-page candy bag.
大结局的剧本长达75页，外加40页的补充内容。

106
00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:03.920
We were only supposed to spend nine days filming this episode, but we ran over, and we actually
我们原本计划用九天时间拍摄这一集，但进度超了，实际上我们

107
00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.260
filmed 10 days.
拍了10天。

108
00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:11.820
We were supposed to finish filming on a Friday, but we had to add a day and film on a Saturday.
我们本应在周五拍完，但不得不加了一天，在周六继续拍摄。

109
00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.140
There was this huge wrap party.
当时有一个盛大的杀青派对。

110
00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.660
I'm sure you remember this, Angela.
安吉拉，我相信你还记得。

111
00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:22.140
Angela planned for Saturday night at this fancy location, and we were like, it'll be fine.
安吉拉把派对定在周六晚上，地点很高级，我们当时觉得，应该没问题。

112
00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:26.180
We'll shoot till about three o'clock, then we'll go get ready for this wrap party.
我们拍到三点左右，然后去准备参加杀青派对。

113
00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.120
There was a red carpet.
现场有红毯。

114
00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:33.160
It was like going to a big fancy movie premiere, but it was a wrap party for our show.
感觉就像去参加一场盛大的电影首映礼，但这只是我们剧组的杀青派对。

115
00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.140
We ended up shooting until 10 p.m.
结果我们一直拍到了晚上10点。

116
00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:36.640
Yeah.
没错。

117
00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.160
The wrap party was on the other side of town.
杀青派对在城的另一边。

118
00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.300
It was like 45 minutes away.
大概有45分钟的车程。

119
00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.380
It started without us.
派对开始的时候我们还没到。

120
00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:48.480
The wrap party started without the cast and crew in the office.
杀青派对开始时，办公室的演职人员还没到场。

121
00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:50.660
It's kind of perfect.
这倒也挺完美的。

122
00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:55.300
I remember when I arrived, they were packing up the red carpet.
我记得我到的时候，他们正在收红毯。

123
00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:02.620
Me, John, and Rain were the last people to walk the red carpet, and I wore a blouse that
我和约翰、雷恩是最后走红毯的人，我穿的那件衬衫是

124
00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:07.760
Pam had worn in the episode on the red carpet because I didn't have clothes.
帕姆在剧里穿过的，因为我当时没带衣服。

125
00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:09.780
I thought I was going home firSt.
我以为我会先回家。

126
00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:10.360
To change.
去换衣服。

127
00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.880
So I borrowed clothes from the costume trailer.
所以我从服装车里借了件衣服。

128
00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.280
The few things they hadn't packed up yet.
那是他们还没打包走的几件衣服之一。

129
00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:19.260
Yeah, I think I got there right before you because the photographers had packed up.
是啊，我想我到得比你早一点，因为摄影师已经收工了。

130
00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.720
And so me and Allie and Brian, I remember we took selfies on the red carpet.
我和艾莉、布莱恩记得我们在红毯上自拍了。

131
00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:24.120
Yeah.
没错。

132
00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.620
So we could have a picture.
这样我们就能留张照片了。

133
00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:31.420
Just so you know, we're going to be breaking down the episode that originally aired.
顺便说一下，我们要解析的是最初播出的版本。

134
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.160
There's kind of two versions out there now.
现在市面上有两个版本。

135
00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:38.320
Yes, the one that aired originally in 2013 is on the DVD.
是的，2013年最初播出的版本收录在DVD里。

136
00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.500
It also plays on Netflix.
Netflix上播放的也是这个版本。

137
00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.180
But there is an iTunes versions that's a two-parter that is different.
但iTunes上有一个两集连播的版本，内容不太一样。

138
00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.800
It's a more trimmed version.
那个版本删减得更多。

139
00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:51.320
In fact, it's missing about seven minutes and 76 seconds of footage.
事实上，它少了大约7分76秒的片段。

140
00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.240
It's also in a slightly different order.
而且场景顺序也略有不同。

141
00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:54.740
Yes.
没错。

142
00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:55.680
Some of the scenes.
部分场景是这样。

143
00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:04.820
So if you are watching with us, know that we are going to be breaking down today and next week the episode as it originally aired.
所以如果你正在和我们一起看，请注意，今天和下周我们将解析的是最初播出的版本。

144
00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:05.260
Yeah.
没错。

145
00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:07.540
That was important to us because it's the finale.
这对我们来说很重要，因为这是大结局。

146
00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:10.680
Well, are we ready for Fast Fact number two?
那么，准备好听第二个冷知识了吗？

147
00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:11.540
We are.
准备好了。

148
00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:15.720
We kind of talked about this last week in AARM part two.
我们上周在《AARM》第二部分里提到过这个。

149
00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:21.060
We talked about how we did our table read for the finale all together and they filmed it.
我们谈到了大家一起为大结局进行剧本围读，而且全程被拍摄了下来。

150
00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:25.780
And before we read the episode, Greg Daniels gave a speech to the cast and crew.
在读剧本之前，格雷格·丹尼尔斯向全体演职人员发表了讲话。

151
00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:30.580
And I rewatched that and I thought it would be really fun to listen to that speech.
我重温了那段视频，觉得听听那段演讲应该会很有意思。

152
00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.440
Yes, it is so good.
没错，真的太棒了。

153
00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.480
We mentioned it in our book even because it's just really special.
我们甚至在书里也提到了它，因为它确实非常特别。

154
00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:38.660
So here you go.
所以，请听吧。

155
00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.020
All right, guys.
好了，各位。

156
00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:42.440
I think everybody's here.
我想大家都到齐了。

157
00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.200
So we'll get started.
那我们就开始吧。

158
00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:49.700
I want to make some last remarks is what this says.
这里写着我想做一些最后的总结发言。

159
00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.240
I'll tell you just a little personal remarks on my part.
我就以个人的身份简单讲几句。

160
00:06:54.480 --> 00:07:00.080
Ten years ago, my agent gave me a tape to watch, VHS tape, of the British office.
十年前，我的经纪人给了我一盘录像带，是英版《办公室》的录像带。

161
00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:01.700
I showed it to my wife.
我给妻子看了。

162
00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:04.200
I said, do you think I should adapt this for the U.S.?
我问她，你觉得我应该把它改编成美版吗？

163
00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.380
She said, absolutely not.
她说，绝对不行。

164
00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.800
But lucky for me, I didn't listen.
但幸运的是，我没听她的。

165
00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:12.880
I've done not much else for ten years.
这十年来，我几乎没做过别的事。

166
00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:17.860
The show has been my passion and my family, literally in many cases.
这部剧一直是我的心血，也是我的家人，在很多情况下确实如此。

167
00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.700
And it's been a privilege to be a part of it.
能参与其中是我的荣幸。

168
00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:23.140
Sad to see it end.
看到它结束真令人难过。

169
00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:29.120
The best part of it all was that it brought me together with the most passionate, talented,
这一切最棒的部分在于，它让我与这间屋子里最热情、最有才华、

170
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.040
funny, dedicated, wonderful group of people, people in this room.
最风趣、最敬业、最棒的一群人聚在了一起。

171
00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:46.280
From Ben and Howard and Terry at the beginning and Allison and Phyllis and Ken and the pilot and the cast assembling
从最初的本、霍华德和特里，到艾莉森、菲利斯和肯，再到试播集，以及演员阵容的集结，

172
00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:52.000
and the writers assembling and the crew assembling and everything just assembled into this fantastic community
编剧团队的集结，剧组人员的集结，一切都汇聚成了这个奇妙的群体，

173
00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:59.340
of like-minded artists who loved combining comedy and poignancy and realism into what became the show.
一群志同道合的艺术家，他们热爱将喜剧、感伤和现实主义结合在一起，成就了这部剧。

174
00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:00.820
And you guys are the beSt.
你们是最棒的。

175
00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.440
Thank you all.
谢谢大家。

176
00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:07.160
I'll say I love you all without falling apart.
我要在不崩溃的情况下说，我爱你们所有人。

177
00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.480
So let's start our last table reading.
那么，让我们开始最后一次剧本围读吧。

178
00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:16.840
Right now, the script is called Finale because we ran out of creativity when we got to the last word.
现在，这个剧本的名字叫《大结局》，因为我们想不出更好的词了。

179
00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:22.340
It was written by me with the enormous contributions of your writing staff this season.
它由我执笔，并得到了本季编剧团队的巨大贡献。

180
00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:23.620
And I'm going to read them.
我要念出他们的名字。

181
00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:24.580
Paul Lieberstein.
保罗·利伯斯坦。

182
00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:28.530
Brent Forrester.
布伦特·福雷斯特。

183
00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:30.470
Dan Sterling.
丹·斯特林。

184
00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:31.790
Allison Silverman.
艾莉森·西尔弗曼。

185
00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.370
Should I slow it down?
我需要念慢点吗？

186
00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:36.230
Warren Lieberstein.
沃伦·利伯斯坦。

187
00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:39.790
Halstead Sullivan.
霍尔斯特德·沙利文。

188
00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:41.470
Gabe Miller.
盖比·米勒。

189
00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:43.410
Jonathan Green.
乔纳森·格林。

190
00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:50.930
Carrie Kemper.
嘉莉·肯珀。

191
00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.310
Nicky Schwartzright.
尼基·施瓦茨赖特。

192
00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:55.010
Charlie Grandy.
查理·格兰迪。

193
00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:56.630
Steve Healy.
史蒂夫·希利。

194
00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:59.110
Robert Padnick.
罗伯特·帕德尼克。

195
00:08:59.330 --> 00:08:59.990
Owen Alexon.
欧文·亚历克森。

196
00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:00.790
Justin Spitzer.
贾斯汀·斯皮策。

197
00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:03.940
That's it, right?
就这些，对吧？

198
00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.080
I think that's it, everyone.
我想就这些了，各位。

199
00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:12.880
Ably assisted by Jay Falk, Jared Ashton, Chris Wood, and Jeff Remsberg.
还有杰伊·福尔克、贾里德·阿什顿、克里斯·伍德和杰夫·雷姆斯伯格的鼎力相助。

200
00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:23.370
This show, like this season, will be produced to the highest level of quality by Steve Burgess.
这部剧，就像这一季一样，将由史蒂夫·伯吉斯以最高水准制作完成。

201
00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:37.320
And it will be put together by the geniuses in post, Dave Rogers, Claire Scanlon, Rob Burnett, and Eric Colgian, one of the others.
后期制作的天才们会把这些素材剪辑在一起，他们是戴夫·罗杰斯、克莱尔·斯坎伦、罗伯·伯内特，还有埃里克·科尔吉安，以及其他几位成员。

202
00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:46.900
I want to name all of our outstanding crew, but for now, let's get one big round of applause and thanks as one championship team.
我想点名感谢我们所有出色的剧组成员，但现在，让我们为这支冠军团队献上最热烈的掌声和谢意。

203
00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:04.330
I'm happy to welcome our NBC guests, Bob Greenblatt, Jen Salke, and everybody from the network.
很高兴欢迎我们的NBC嘉宾，鲍勃·格林布拉特、詹·萨尔克，以及来自电视台的各位朋友。

204
00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:05.370
Thank you for coming.
感谢你们的到来。

205
00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:13.520
And finally, I'm very happy and proud to have Ken Quapis back to direct our finale.
最后，我非常高兴且自豪地请回了肯·夸皮斯来执导我们的结局篇。

206
00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:25.020
Ken was the country vet who birthed this puppy, and now he's going to put it down.
肯是当年接生这只“小狗”的乡村兽医，现在他要负责送它最后一程了。

207
00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:34.300
Really looking forward to spending the next eight or nine days on the set with you all.
非常期待在接下来的八九天里与大家一起在片场度过。

208
00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:36.100
No one I'd rather have there than Ken.
除了肯，我不想让任何人来做这件事。

209
00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:37.440
Okay, brace yourselves.
好了，做好心理准备。

210
00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.300
It's going to get very sentimental in here.
这里马上要变得非常感伤了。

211
00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.400
Well, I love listening to that again.
听着这些录音，感觉真好。

212
00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:43.640
Me too.
我也是。

213
00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.400
Actually, I watched the whole table read.
其实，我把整个剧本围读会都看了一遍。

214
00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:47.340
You did?
真的吗？

215
00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:48.020
I did.
是的。

216
00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:48.880
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

217
00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:51.700
I mean, I'm glad I did.
我是说，我很高兴我看了。

218
00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:52.960
It was really special.
那真的很特别。

219
00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.880
We were a mess.
我们当时都乱成一团了。

220
00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:02.380
Well, one of the things I love in listening to that is hearing Greg acknowledge everybody.
听着这些录音，我最喜欢的一点就是听到格雷格对每个人的肯定。

221
00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:06.560
That was always very important to him, to give everybody their moment of acknowledgement.
这对他来说一直很重要，他想给每个人属于他们的闪光时刻。

222
00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:11.340
And he went on after that to then name every single cast member.
在那之后，他接着念出了每一位演员的名字。

223
00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:12.120
That's right.
没错。

224
00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:13.340
And people applauded.
大家也都鼓掌了。

225
00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.820
He's a special person.
他是个特别的人。

226
00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:15.280
Yeah.
是啊。

227
00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:23.100
Well, Steve Burgess told me that after this table read, we did not have a locked script
史蒂夫·伯吉斯告诉我，在这次围读会之后，我们的剧本直到拍摄第四天

228
00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.540
until the fourth day of shooting.
才最终定稿。

229
00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:32.600
He said for the first three or four days, Greg would turn in pages late at night the night
他说在前三四天里，格雷格都是在拍摄前一天

230
00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.000
before.
深夜才交稿。

231
00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:36.340
We used both of our first ADs on this one.
我们这次动用了两位第一副导演。

232
00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:40.600
Kelly would figure out how to schedule the next day, and Rusty would run the set.
凯利负责安排第二天的拍摄计划，而拉斯蒂负责现场调度。

233
00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:44.800
It wasn't until about that fourth day that Greg finally turned over a whole script.
直到第四天左右，格雷格才终于交出了完整的剧本。

234
00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:49.540
I think he was, and he said he was having a hard time calling it finished.
我觉得他当时确实很难下定决心说剧本完成了。

235
00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:49.940
Yeah.
是啊。

236
00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:50.580
You know?
你懂的吧？

237
00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:51.420
All right.
好吧。

238
00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.860
So now, Angela, you have our Fast Pack 3.
那么现在，安吉拉，你有我们的“快件3号”。

239
00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:55.080
I do.
是的，我有。

240
00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:59.860
Y'all, I've got some good digital clutter for this time while we were filming.
大家，我整理了一些拍摄期间的数字杂物。

241
00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:04.220
I have a few things I want to share in this Fast Pack and some more for next week.
在这个“快件”里我有一些东西想分享，下周还有更多。

242
00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:04.920
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

243
00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:09.360
Angela has a little smile on her face because I think I don't know what's coming.
安吉拉脸上露出了微笑，因为我想她不知道接下来会是什么。

244
00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.920
You know one thing but not the other.
你知道其中一件，但不知道另一件。

245
00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:12.380
Okay.
好吧。

246
00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:14.540
I'm going to start with the thing you don't know.
我先从你不知道的那件开始说起。

247
00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:20.700
I found an email that I wrote to Steve Carell during this time, and I want to read it to
我翻到了一封我当时写给史蒂夫·卡瑞尔的邮件，我想读给

248
00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:20.860
you.
你听。

249
00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:21.260
Okay.
好的。

250
00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:22.520
Hey, Steve.
嘿，史蒂夫。

251
00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:23.600
How the heck are you?
你到底怎么样了？

252
00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:26.080
You have been on my mind a lot lately.
最近我经常想起你。

253
00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:30.080
We had our table read yesterday for our second-to-last episode ever.
昨天我们进行了倒数第二集的剧本围读。

254
00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:32.020
We are really feeling it.
我们真的很有感触。

255
00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:36.600
Kate started to cry the other day when a group of us were talking about our crew wrap gift.
前几天我们一群人在讨论剧组杀青礼物时，凯特就开始哭了。

256
00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:41.200
Then Jenna teared up at the table read, and then I was filming this emotional scene where
然后珍娜在围读时也热泪盈眶，接着我在拍一场情感戏，

257
00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.100
I confide to Oscar that I love Dwight.
戏里我向奥斯卡吐露我爱着德怀特。

258
00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:47.340
I cried a little each take, and then Jeff Blitz walks up to me and whispers in my ear,
每拍一条我都会掉点眼泪，然后杰夫·布里茨走过来在我耳边低语，

259
00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:49.820
pretend to say goodbye to the whole show in this take.
让我在这条里假装是在跟整部剧告别。

260
00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:09.020
Oh, also, I've been working on a scrapbook for everyone and going through all of these
哦，对了，我一直在为大家制作剪贴簿，翻看过去九年里的所有

261
00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:12.000
old photos from the last nine years and getting so nostalgic.
老照片，真是感慨万千。

262
00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:17.400
Today on set, John talked about his last scene with you when Jim walks into Michael's office.
今天在片场，约翰谈到了他和你最后的那场戏，就是吉姆走进迈克尔办公室的那场。

263
00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.300
He said he just broke down.
他说他当时直接崩溃了。

264
00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:24.180
I mean, we've all been so incredibly fortunate to be together and truly care about each other
我是说，我们所有人都极其幸运能聚在一起，并且在这些年里

265
00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:25.140
all these years.
真心关怀彼此。

266
00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:29.860
I think about you and how difficult those last few weeks must have been from your perspective.
我常想到你，想到从你的角度来看，最后那几周一定非常难熬。

267
00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:32.480
I comprehend it on a whole different level now.
我现在从一个完全不同的层面理解了这一点。

268
00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:37.860
And of course, I cannot email you without including some family updates, so here are some pictures.
当然，我给你发邮件肯定少不了要更新一下家里的近况，所以这里有一些照片。

269
00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:41.080
The first one is of Isabel and Jenna's little boy.
第一张是伊莎贝尔和珍娜的小男孩。

270
00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:43.020
We ran into each other at Target.
我们在塔吉特百货偶遇了。

271
00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:43.800
Go figure.
真没想到。

272
00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:48.360
I love that our kids are growing up together.
我很高兴我们的孩子能一起长大。

273
00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:51.520
I told Jenna maybe they'll get married and then we'll be related.
我跟珍娜说，也许他们以后会结婚，那我们就是亲家了。

274
00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:52.080
Ha ha!
哈哈！

275
00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:59.300
Oh, and Jenna booked a play in New York City, so she'll be there this spring and summer.
哦，珍娜接了一部纽约的舞台剧，所以今年春夏她会在那里。

276
00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.480
I am so excited for her.
我真为她感到高兴。

277
00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:04.660
The second picture is of Isabel and our dog, Biscuit.
第二张照片是伊莎贝尔和我们的狗，饼干。

278
00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:06.860
Isabel is such a big girl now.
伊莎贝尔现在长成大姑娘了。

279
00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.600
I can't believe she'll be five in May.
真不敢相信她五月份就五岁了。

280
00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:11.060
She is my favorite person to be with always.
她一直是我最喜欢待在一起的人。

281
00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.900
Her latest craze is hip-hop class.
她最近迷上了嘻哈课。

282
00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.960
She didn't like ballet, but she loves hip-hop.
她不喜欢芭蕾，但她超爱嘻哈。

283
00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:20.700
And the last picture is of Oscar and Ursula's sweet little girl.
最后一张照片是奥斯卡和乌苏拉可爱的女儿。

284
00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:23.380
She is five months old and came to visit on set.
她才五个月大，还来片场探过班。

285
00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:25.420
Being a dad really suits Oscar.
当爸爸真的很适合奥斯卡。

286
00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:27.580
He is exhausted but happy.
他虽然精疲力竭，但很幸福。

287
00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:30.840
Oh, and Rain's son came to our table read this week.
哦，雷恩的儿子这周也来了我们的剧本围读。

288
00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:33.900
He is such an amazing combination of Rain and Holly.
他简直是雷恩和霍莉的完美结合体。

289
00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:35.740
And oh my God, so tall.
天哪，他长得好高。

290
00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.520
He is almost my height.
他都快跟我一样高了。

291
00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:40.700
I know that's not saying much, but he's only nine.
我知道这没啥好比的，但他才九岁啊。

292
00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:44.380
Okay, that's it for now.
好了，先这样吧。

293
00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:45.560
I miss you and Nancy.
我很想你和南希。

294
00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:49.480
I went through so many pictures of you guys in my scrapbook and I smiled a lot.
我在剪贴簿里翻看了很多你们的照片，看了之后我笑了好久。

295
00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:53.900
At some point, we need to all get together for a dinner or get the kids together for a hangout.
找个时间，我们得聚在一起吃顿饭，或者让孩子们聚聚。

296
00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:55.420
Love ya, Ange.
爱你，安吉。

297
00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:58.300
So here's what I'm thinking as you're reading that.
所以当你读到那封邮件时，我是这么想的。

298
00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:06.280
You are writing him this email and you have no idea that he is going to come surprise you on set.
你正在给他写这封邮件，却完全不知道他会去片场给你一个惊喜。

299
00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:07.100
I know!
我知道！

300
00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:09.960
So you're like, I better bring him in.
所以你的反应是，我最好还是让他进来吧。

301
00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.380
Like, this is so your personality.
真的，这太符合你的个性了。

302
00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:15.180
You're like, well, I don't want Steve to feel left out of this finale moment.
你当时想，嗯，我不想让史蒂夫觉得他被排除在这个大结局时刻之外。

303
00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:17.220
I'm going to write him this great email.
我要给他写一封很棒的邮件。

304
00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:18.520
It's such a beautiful email.
那是一封非常感人的邮件。

305
00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:22.780
And he's reading that and he's thinking, Ange, I'm going to see you in a few days.
他读着邮件心想，安吉，我过几天就能见到你了。

306
00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:23.480
I know!
我知道！

307
00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:25.320
But of course, he didn't give it away.
但当然，他没有说漏嘴。

308
00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:29.940
He wrote me back a lovely response, you know, and said, oh, I bet it's really tough right now.
他给我回了一封很可爱的邮件，你知道的，他说，哦，我敢说现在一定很难熬吧。

309
00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:30.920
I remember that.
我记得那件事。

310
00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:31.480
Yeah!
是啊！

311
00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:33.780
