看来确实不是。

532
00:29:40.860 --> 00:29:43.060
Well, let's get into it.
好吧，我们开始吧。

533
00:29:43.240 --> 00:29:46.460
We open on Dwight driving in his car.
开场是德怀特开车。

534
00:29:46.720 --> 00:29:50.400
He's speaking to a documentary crew member.
他正在和纪录片摄制组的一名成员说话。

535
00:29:50.620 --> 00:29:51.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

536
00:29:51.340 --> 00:29:55.940
And he's explaining that the documentary series finished airing about a year ago.
他解释说纪录片系列大约在一年前播完了。

537
00:29:56.480 --> 00:29:59.140
And he's kind of like, why are you sending another crew?
他大概是说，你们为什么又派人来？

538
00:29:59.240 --> 00:30:00.240
Why are you filming us again?
你们为什么又要拍我们？

539
00:30:00.240 --> 00:30:00.440
Yeah.
是啊。

540
00:30:00.460 --> 00:30:01.140
Why are you here?
你们为什么在这儿？

541
00:30:01.260 --> 00:30:01.820
This is done.
这事儿已经结束了。

542
00:30:02.040 --> 00:30:05.840
And the documentary person says we're getting bonus footage for the DVD.
然后纪录片工作人员说我们是在为DVD拍摄花絮素材。

543
00:30:05.840 --> 00:30:10.460
And then Dwight says, oh, nobody buys DVDs anymore.
接着德怀特说，哦，现在没人买DVD了。

544
00:30:10.740 --> 00:30:13.680
And of course, I'm like, this lady's watching it on a DVD.
当然，我当时就在想，这位女士正在用DVD看这部剧呢。

545
00:30:13.980 --> 00:30:14.500
That's right.
没错。

546
00:30:14.760 --> 00:30:19.900
The voice you hear is our longtime camera operator and sometimes director, Matt Sohn.
你听到的那个声音是我们长期的摄影师，有时也担任导演的马特·索恩。

547
00:30:19.900 --> 00:30:24.900
He just did these lines temporarily because he was the person sitting in the car with Rain.
他只是临时录了这些台词，因为当时是他坐在车里和雷恩在一起。

548
00:30:25.140 --> 00:30:29.860
And the plan was always that we were going to replace his voice with Dave Rogers, who has been...
原本的计划是我们要用戴夫·罗杰斯的声音替换掉他，戴夫一直都是……

549
00:30:29.860 --> 00:30:31.420
The documentary person.
那个纪录片工作人员。

550
00:30:31.420 --> 00:30:34.960
But Greg really liked having Matt's voice on the show.
但格雷格真的很喜欢马特的声音出现在剧里。

551
00:30:35.100 --> 00:30:35.500
Aw.
噢。

552
00:30:35.660 --> 00:30:36.500
So they kept it.
所以他们留下了它。

553
00:30:36.640 --> 00:30:37.240
Love it.
太棒了。

554
00:30:37.820 --> 00:30:41.140
Well, let's just talk a second about the new car Dwight has.
好吧，我们来聊聊德怀特的新车。

555
00:30:41.300 --> 00:30:51.300
He has traded in his 1987 Pontiac Firebird Trans Am to a 2012 header orange Dodge Challenger SRT8.
他把那辆1987年的庞蒂亚克火鸟Trans Am换成了一辆2012年亮橙色的道奇挑战者SRT8。

556
00:30:51.700 --> 00:30:52.000
Rawr.
吼。

557
00:30:52.460 --> 00:30:54.240
I guess this is his manager car.
我想这就是他的经理座驾吧。

558
00:30:54.420 --> 00:30:54.720
Yeah.
没错。

559
00:30:54.960 --> 00:30:55.440
Spicy.
够辣。

560
00:30:55.440 --> 00:30:59.940
As he's driving, we notice a couple signs along the way.
当他开车时，我们注意到路边有几个牌子。

561
00:31:00.140 --> 00:31:01.980
They're election signs.
那是竞选标语牌。

562
00:31:02.460 --> 00:31:02.720
Yes.
是的。

563
00:31:03.020 --> 00:31:06.320
And one of them says Oscar Martinez is running for state senator.
其中一个写着奥斯卡·马丁内斯正在竞选州参议员。

564
00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:12.720
Dwight explains that they have regained a number of lost clients, including the White Pages.
德怀特解释说他们已经挽回了一些流失的客户，包括白页电话簿公司。

565
00:31:13.320 --> 00:31:16.240
He says he's getting married tomorrow afternoon.
他说他明天下午要结婚了。

566
00:31:16.260 --> 00:31:18.860
They're doing a little mini reunion in the morning.
他们早上会举行一个小型的重聚活动。

567
00:31:19.040 --> 00:31:22.940
And this is when we find out that he's fired Kevin.
就在这时我们发现他解雇了凯文。

568
00:31:22.940 --> 00:31:26.600
Yeah, he hasn't seen Kevin since he let him go.
没错，自从解雇凯文后，他就没再见过他。

569
00:31:26.900 --> 00:31:35.180
This flashes back to the conference room, and Dwight wheels in a trolley of three big cakes and some blue icing.
镜头闪回到会议室，德怀特推着一辆装有三个大蛋糕和一些蓝色糖霜的手推车进来。

570
00:31:35.360 --> 00:31:39.360
And I guess the way you get fired now is you get your name on a cake.
我想现在被解雇的方式就是名字被写在蛋糕上。

571
00:31:39.440 --> 00:31:41.460
Or if you're Toby, you just get a squiggle.
或者如果你是托比，就只有一个乱涂的符号。

572
00:31:41.820 --> 00:31:43.240
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是这样。

573
00:31:43.940 --> 00:31:46.380
Or also retired, you get a cake.
或者退休了，也会有一个蛋糕。

574
00:31:46.580 --> 00:31:49.720
Yes, we find out that Stanley is leaving as well.
是的，我们发现斯坦利也要走了。

575
00:31:49.720 --> 00:31:53.260
Well, he's been looking for it to this day since he was 18 years old.
嗯，他说他从18岁起就一直盼着这一天。

576
00:31:53.680 --> 00:31:56.180
Is that how long he's been at Dunder Mifflin?
他在邓德·米夫林待了那么久吗？

577
00:31:56.780 --> 00:31:57.200
No.
不是。

578
00:31:57.440 --> 00:31:57.720
No.
不是。

579
00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:03.120
I think he's just saying that he's been a working man since he was 18 years old.
我想他只是在说他从18岁起就开始工作了。

580
00:32:03.240 --> 00:32:03.420
Yeah.
没错。

581
00:32:03.620 --> 00:32:07.000
I would like to point out something for my background catch, folks.
我想为我的背景细节指出一点，各位。

582
00:32:07.700 --> 00:32:17.080
When Dwight starts to fire Kevin, if you watch my face, I played it as if I knew this was coming, that maybe Dwight had told me this was happening today.
当德怀特开始解雇凯文时，如果你看我的表情，我演得好像我知道这件事要发生，也许是德怀特提前告诉了我今天会发生什么。

583
00:32:17.340 --> 00:32:19.300
And there's a little bit of pleasure.
而且带有一点点愉悦。

584
00:32:20.260 --> 00:32:22.540
There's a little bit of happiness on my face.
我的脸上有一丝快乐。

585
00:32:22.920 --> 00:32:24.080
Well, it makes sense.
嗯，这说得通。

586
00:32:24.220 --> 00:32:27.260
I mean, I think you've been redoing Kevin's work for a long time.
我是说，我觉得你已经帮凯文重做工作很久了。

587
00:32:28.140 --> 00:32:33.960
Before we leave the conference room, I did want to just revisit this painting that's behind Dwight.
在离开会议室之前，我确实想再看看德怀特身后的那幅画。

588
00:32:35.060 --> 00:32:41.680
I was wondering if anyone out there knows how many paintings of Dwight there are in the series.
我很好奇有没有人知道这部剧里到底有多少幅德怀特的画像。

589
00:32:41.720 --> 00:32:43.260
I know there's one in Dwight K.
我知道在《德怀特·K·

590
00:32:43.380 --> 00:32:44.320
Schrute, Acting Manager.
施鲁特，代理经理》那一集里有一幅。

591
00:32:44.480 --> 00:32:45.360
It's a different one.
那是另一幅。

592
00:32:45.480 --> 00:32:46.040
A portrait.
一幅肖像画。

593
00:32:46.180 --> 00:32:47.340
A portrait by reception.
前台旁边的一幅肖像画。

594
00:32:47.920 --> 00:32:50.940
Then there's the one of him and Moe's that hangs in his office.
然后还有那幅他和莫斯挂在他办公室里的画。

595
00:32:51.140 --> 00:32:52.100
Then there's this one.
接着就是这一幅。

596
00:32:52.100 --> 00:33:00.860
And I think we should all note that Angela and Dwight both love giant portraits of themselves because she had one in her house with the senator.
而且我认为我们都应该注意到，安吉拉和德怀特都喜欢自己的巨幅肖像，因为她和参议员住的时候家里就有一幅。

597
00:33:00.980 --> 00:33:07.000
So I like to believe now in their home together, lady, that they have a massive painting of the two of them.
所以我愿意相信现在在他们共同的家里，女士，他们挂着一幅巨大的两人合影油画。

598
00:33:07.260 --> 00:33:07.740
Yes.
是的。

599
00:33:07.920 --> 00:33:08.780
As you walk in.
一进门就能看到。

600
00:33:08.940 --> 00:33:10.720
With baby Philip, I'm sure.
肯定还有小菲利普在上面。

601
00:33:10.900 --> 00:33:11.180
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

602
00:33:11.320 --> 00:33:12.340
Will be in it.
会参与其中的。

603
00:33:12.560 --> 00:33:12.780
Yeah.
是啊。

604
00:33:13.400 --> 00:33:15.560
Maybe some angels flying over.
也许会有天使飞过。

605
00:33:16.920 --> 00:33:23.360
Have you ever gone to the mall and seen where they'll do sort of like a portrait of your family?
你去过商场吗？见过那种给全家人画肖像画的地方吗？

606
00:33:23.560 --> 00:33:26.700
I think they do it as a picture, but then they make it look like a painting.
我想他们是先拍张照，然后处理成油画的样子。

607
00:33:26.820 --> 00:33:27.720
They make it look like a painting.
让他们看起来像幅油画。

608
00:33:27.920 --> 00:33:28.280
Yes.
是的。

609
00:33:28.460 --> 00:33:35.100
I mean, I have a very good friend of my mom's that if you go in her house, she's got a big one of her family.
我是说，我妈妈有个很好的朋友，你去她家的话，会看到她挂着一幅巨大的全家福。

610
00:33:35.220 --> 00:33:40.740
But they all look a little – it's like a Monet.
但他们看起来都有点……就像莫奈的画一样。

611
00:33:41.440 --> 00:33:46.300
Like the further away you are, the more they look like themselves.
离得越远，看起来越像他们本人。

612
00:33:46.880 --> 00:33:47.360
Oh.
噢。

613
00:33:47.360 --> 00:33:49.720
And then the closer you get, it's a bunch of dots.
然后你走近看，就是一堆点点。

614
00:33:50.040 --> 00:33:50.360
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

615
00:33:50.880 --> 00:33:51.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

616
00:33:51.700 --> 00:34:00.460
I wonder if there would ever be a time in my life when I would feel comfortable having a giant portrait of myself hanging in my home.
我在想，我这辈子会不会有那么一个时刻，会觉得在家里挂一幅巨大的个人肖像画是很自然的事。

617
00:34:01.800 --> 00:34:03.780
Is it something I should work toward?
这是我应该努力追求的目标吗？

618
00:34:04.220 --> 00:34:06.860
Or is it something to be avoided?
还是说应该尽量避免？

619
00:34:08.400 --> 00:34:09.680
Cassie's shaking her head.
凯西在摇头。

620
00:34:09.680 --> 00:34:11.900
And she's like, do not work toward this goal.
她那表情就像在说，千万别把这当目标。

621
00:34:12.980 --> 00:34:17.060
Well, we are going to have a portrait of ourselves as John Wick, thanks to Sam.
好吧，多亏了萨姆，我们马上就要有我们扮演“疾速追杀”角色的肖像画了。

622
00:34:17.180 --> 00:34:17.760
This is true.
确实如此。

623
00:34:17.960 --> 00:34:19.400
These are the portraits we want.
这才是我们想要的肖像画。

624
00:34:19.400 --> 00:34:20.280
This is what we want.
这就是我们想要的。

625
00:34:21.160 --> 00:34:22.180
We did it.
我们做到了。

626
00:34:22.720 --> 00:34:25.160
Well, now we're going to cut to present day.
好了，现在我们要切回现实时间了。

627
00:34:25.420 --> 00:34:27.400
And Jim is biking into work.
吉姆正骑车去上班。

628
00:34:27.400 --> 00:34:32.660
And he's going to join the rest of us who are following Dwight in some form of Tai Chi.
他要去加入我们其余人的行列，跟着德怀特一起练某种太极。

629
00:34:32.940 --> 00:34:33.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

630
00:34:33.840 --> 00:34:35.980
We got a fan mail flurry about this.
我们收到了很多关于这部分的粉丝来信。

631
00:34:36.320 --> 00:34:37.400
Where do I begin?
从哪儿说起呢？

632
00:34:37.400 --> 00:34:38.720
Connor H.
康纳·H。

633
00:34:38.940 --> 00:34:41.140
from Fishers, Indiana, and many others.
来自印第安纳州费希尔斯，还有许多其他人。

634
00:34:41.420 --> 00:34:43.920
Also, Angela Kaysen and a bull**** card.
还有安吉拉·凯森和一张胡扯的卡片。

635
00:34:44.100 --> 00:34:44.540
Oh.
噢。

636
00:34:44.740 --> 00:34:46.480
So include that in your liSt.
所以把那个也加进你的名单里。

637
00:34:47.000 --> 00:34:51.640
Well, Connor said in the finale, Jim says he now rides his bike to work.
好吧，康纳说在结局里，吉姆说他现在骑自行车上班。

638
00:34:51.640 --> 00:34:57.340
First of all, did he get over his sweatiness from when he biked to work in Stanford?
首先，他克服了当年在斯坦福骑车上班时容易出汗的问题了吗？

639
00:34:58.140 --> 00:35:03.660
Second, he says that it saves on gas, but it appears that Pam drove to work before him.
其次，他说这样能省油钱，但看起来帕姆比他先开车去上班了。

640
00:35:03.800 --> 00:35:05.380
So does it really save on gas?
所以这真的能省油钱吗？

641
00:35:05.600 --> 00:35:06.860
And then Rebecca E.
然后是丽贝卡·E。

642
00:35:07.040 --> 00:35:13.240
from Sugarland says, I guess Pam is entirely in charge of dropping their kids off at school or daycare.
来自舒格兰，她说，我猜帕姆完全负责送孩子们去学校或托儿所。

643
00:35:13.240 --> 00:35:17.400
It really makes me question what Jim means by saving on gas.
这真的让我怀疑吉姆说的省油钱到底是什么意思。

644
00:35:17.640 --> 00:35:19.560
I had so many questions about this.
关于这一点我有很多疑问。

645
00:35:19.720 --> 00:35:19.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

646
00:35:20.500 --> 00:35:23.640
I would have loved to seen them ride in together on a tandem bike.
我真希望能看到他们骑着双人自行车一起去上班。

647
00:35:24.100 --> 00:35:24.260
What?
什么？

648
00:35:24.560 --> 00:35:25.760
That's ridiculous.
那太荒谬了。

649
00:35:26.240 --> 00:35:30.980
No, because if they're going to commit to bike riding, they need to do it together.
不，因为如果他们决定要骑车，就得一起骑。

650
00:35:30.980 --> 00:35:34.160
If they really want to, like, help save money on gas.
如果他们真的想，比如，帮着省点油钱的话。

651
00:35:34.160 --> 00:35:40.360
Also, my bull**** card is that Pam has to do all these, like, tai chi yoga moves in high heels.
还有，我的“胡扯卡”是关于帕姆必须穿着高跟鞋做那些太极瑜伽动作。

652
00:35:41.100 --> 00:35:42.420
Oh, I see.
哦，我明白了。

653
00:35:42.540 --> 00:35:43.280
That's not cool.
那太不厚道了。

654
00:35:43.560 --> 00:35:45.720
Your bull**** card was not about the bike riding.
你的“胡扯卡”不是关于骑自行车的。

655
00:35:45.880 --> 00:35:46.120
Oh, no, no, no.
哦，不，不，不。

656
00:35:46.120 --> 00:35:46.920
It was about the exercise.
是关于锻炼的。

657
00:35:46.940 --> 00:35:47.760
No, it's a combo.
不，那是组合拳。

658
00:35:47.960 --> 00:35:48.540
Oh, it's a combo.
哦，是组合拳。

659
00:35:48.600 --> 00:35:49.780
Combo bull**** card.
组合型“胡扯卡”。

660
00:35:49.900 --> 00:35:50.240
I see.
我明白了。

661
00:35:50.320 --> 00:35:51.480
It's a new bull**** card.
这是张新出的“胡扯卡”。

662
00:35:51.700 --> 00:35:51.780
Oh.
哦。

663
00:35:51.780 --> 00:35:52.640
It, like, folds out.
它还能折叠展开。

664
00:35:52.840 --> 00:35:53.160
It's a...
它是个……

665
00:35:53.760 --> 00:35:54.200
Okay.
好吧。

666
00:35:54.880 --> 00:35:56.760
Well, Jim has a talking head now.
吉姆现在有个访谈镜头。

667
00:35:56.920 --> 00:35:58.960
He says he and Pam are great.
他说他和帕姆好着呢。

668
00:35:59.200 --> 00:35:59.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

669
00:35:59.620 --> 00:36:03.300
And she just recently finished her mural for the Irish Cultural Center.
而且她最近刚完成了为爱尔兰文化中心画的壁画。

670
00:36:03.300 --> 00:36:05.780
Yeah, and then we flashed to that moment.
没错，然后我们就闪回到那个瞬间。

671
00:36:06.160 --> 00:36:08.080
There's a bunch of people gathered around.
有一群人围在那里。

672
00:36:08.360 --> 00:36:09.560
Her children are there.
她的孩子们也在场。

673
00:36:09.940 --> 00:36:11.640
Let me tell you where we shot that.
我来告诉你我们在哪拍的那个镜头。

674
00:36:11.820 --> 00:36:14.540
The far side of the Dunder Mifflin parking lot.
在邓德·米夫林停车场的另一头。

675
00:36:14.960 --> 00:36:16.000
Against the bushes.
靠着灌木丛那边。

676
00:36:16.160 --> 00:36:17.740
They put a big mural up.
他们立起了一面大壁画。

677
00:36:17.840 --> 00:36:19.080
They put me on a scaffold.
他们把我架在脚手架上。

678
00:36:19.400 --> 00:36:23.000
They put some background actors down in the parking lot looking up.
他们找了一些群演在停车场下面抬头看。

679
00:36:23.140 --> 00:36:25.420
Like on the side where the warehouse door was?
就像仓库门那边的那一侧吗？

680
00:36:25.540 --> 00:36:26.840
No, the other side.
不，是另一侧。

681
00:36:27.180 --> 00:36:31.020
Like as if you're walking to our set from one building to another.
就像你从一栋楼走到我们片场那样。

682
00:36:31.200 --> 00:36:32.620
Oh, that was true parking lot.
哦，那是真正的停车场。

683
00:36:32.620 --> 00:36:33.720
Total parking lot.
完全就是停车场。

684
00:36:34.080 --> 00:36:38.060
I'll never forget it because I was slightly terrified standing up there.
我永远忘不了，因为站在上面我有点害怕。

685
00:36:38.140 --> 00:36:38.820
I don't know why.
我也不知道为什么。

686
00:36:38.940 --> 00:36:40.120
It was very wobbly.
它晃得厉害。

687
00:36:40.280 --> 00:36:44.160
I would say the two characters that spent the most time up in the air are you and Dwight.
我觉得在空中待的时间最长的两个角色就是你和德怀特。

688
00:36:44.340 --> 00:36:45.120
And you know what?
你知道吗？

689
00:36:45.200 --> 00:36:46.460
I don't care for it.
我可不喜欢那样。

690
00:36:46.680 --> 00:36:46.860
Yeah.
是啊。

691
00:36:47.600 --> 00:36:50.500
It just makes me squeamish.
那让我感到很不舒服。

692
00:36:50.680 --> 00:36:50.860
Yeah.
是啊。

693
00:36:51.060 --> 00:36:52.740
I prefer being on the ground.
我更喜欢脚踏实地。

694
00:36:52.880 --> 00:36:53.220
Yeah, same.
我也是。

695
00:36:54.080 --> 00:36:56.480
Now there's a scene between Pam and Angela.
现在有一场帕姆和安吉拉的戏。

696
00:36:57.020 --> 00:36:58.960
They're doing their movements together.
她们在一起做动作。

697
00:36:59.360 --> 00:37:01.780
And Pam was like, Angela, are you ready for the wedding?
帕姆说，安吉拉，你准备好迎接婚礼了吗？

698
00:37:02.020 --> 00:37:06.700
And you think for a minute that Angela has really turned a corner with her snarkiness.
你有一瞬间会觉得安吉拉的刻薄真的有所收敛了。

699
00:37:07.060 --> 00:37:09.240
She says, oh, my heart is so open.
她说，哦，我的心是如此敞开。

700
00:37:09.540 --> 00:37:10.800
I'm so at peace.
我感到无比平静。

701
00:37:10.940 --> 00:37:12.620
And then she goes, ugh, look at Meredith.
然后她说，呃，看看梅雷迪思。

702
00:37:12.840 --> 00:37:14.000
She's disgusting.
她真恶心。

703
00:37:14.660 --> 00:37:16.680
Like just instant snark.
就像那种瞬间的讽刺。

704
00:37:16.680 --> 00:37:20.780
But then we cut to Meredith and she looks completely different.
但随后镜头切到梅雷迪思，她看起来完全变了样。

705
00:37:21.080 --> 00:37:22.140
Her hair is different.
她的发型变了。

706
00:37:22.300 --> 00:37:23.580
It's like longer.
好像变长了。

707
00:37:23.580 --> 00:37:24.580
It's brown.
是棕色的。

708
00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:29.620
She is not wearing her usual kind of crazy jumper.
她没穿平时那种古怪的套头衫。

709
00:37:30.160 --> 00:37:30.220
Yeah.
没错。

710
00:37:30.620 --> 00:37:31.100
Yeah.
是啊。

711
00:37:31.320 --> 00:37:33.460
And there's a talking head that explains why.
还有一段采访解释了原因。

712
00:37:33.680 --> 00:37:34.060
That's right.
没错。

713
00:37:34.160 --> 00:37:35.200
It's in deleted scenes.
是在删减片段里。

714
00:37:35.400 --> 00:37:35.940
Let's hear it.
我们来听听看。

715
00:37:48.480 --> 00:37:53.260
If you watch it when she says, now I'm in these yoga pants, Kate, like kicks her leg
如果你看那一段，当她说“我现在穿的是这种瑜伽裤，凯特”，然后把腿

716
00:37:53.260 --> 00:37:54.060
up way out.
高高地踢起来。

717
00:37:54.200 --> 00:37:55.600
Like she's so bendy.
她身体好柔软。

718
00:37:56.280 --> 00:37:58.900
But I love that Meredith is now a vegan.
但我喜欢梅雷迪思现在成了素食主义者这一点。

719
00:37:59.120 --> 00:38:00.160
She's doing yoga.
她在练瑜伽。

720
00:38:00.800 --> 00:38:01.240
Yeah.
是啊。

721
00:38:01.520 --> 00:38:03.940
She looks like she might go to a tanning bed.
她看起来像是会去晒日光浴。

722
00:38:04.500 --> 00:38:08.160
That sort of goes against her new healthy lifestyle though, huh?
但这似乎和她新的健康生活方式相悖，对吧？

723
00:38:08.300 --> 00:38:08.500
Maybe so.
也许吧。

724
00:38:08.640 --> 00:38:08.860
Yeah.
是啊。

725
00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:11.200
Maybe she's just spending more time outdoors.
也许她只是花更多时间在户外。

726
00:38:11.420 --> 00:38:12.100
Vitamin D.
补充维生素D。

727
00:38:12.300 --> 00:38:12.520
Yeah.
没错。

728
00:38:12.660 --> 00:38:13.040
Fitness.
健身。

729
00:38:13.320 --> 00:38:13.500
Fitness.
健身。

730
00:38:14.200 --> 00:38:16.820
Now there's a very sweet moment between Dwight and Angela.
现在德怀特和安吉拉之间有一个非常甜蜜的时刻。

731
00:38:17.280 --> 00:38:17.720
Yes.
是的。

732
00:38:18.180 --> 00:38:20.120
Angela's going to run up and give him a kiss.
安吉拉跑过去给了他一个吻。

733
00:38:20.120 --> 00:38:22.940
And she's just so excited about their wedding.
她对他们的婚礼感到非常兴奋。

734
00:38:22.940 --> 00:38:26.740
And he feels a little sad because some of the old gang aren't there.
而他感到有点难过，因为一些老朋友不在场。

735
00:38:26.880 --> 00:38:27.580
And she's like, you know what?
她说，你知道吗？

736
00:38:27.580 --> 00:38:28.420
It's going to be perfect.
一切都会很完美的。

737
00:38:28.740 --> 00:38:29.700
Just me and you.
就我们俩。

738
00:38:29.860 --> 00:38:30.740
That's all we need.
这就足够了。

739
00:38:30.740 --> 00:38:36.580
And then he brings up this man that's been, I guess, growing cheese for him since the day
然后他提到了那个男人，我想，从他出生那天起就一直在为他制作奶酪，

740
00:38:36.580 --> 00:38:39.820
of his birth and that he's going to feed them cheese.
而且他打算用奶酪招待他们。

741
00:38:40.100 --> 00:38:41.220
Growing cheese?
制作奶酪？

742
00:38:41.600 --> 00:38:42.500
Fermenting cheese?
发酵奶酪？

743
00:38:42.760 --> 00:38:42.980
Yeah.
对。

744
00:38:43.980 --> 00:38:44.540
What?
什么？

745
00:38:44.900 --> 00:38:46.620
What shrewd custom is this?
这是什么精明的习俗？

746
00:38:46.840 --> 00:38:47.400
Okay.
好吧。

747
00:38:47.600 --> 00:38:49.920
I do have one little story though about this scene.
不过关于这个场景我有一个小故事。

748
00:38:50.120 --> 00:38:50.500
Okay.
好的。

749
00:38:50.820 --> 00:38:55.140
For my background catch people, when we're doing the morning stretches.
对于那些关注背景细节的人，当我们做晨间拉伸时。

750
00:38:55.520 --> 00:38:55.700
Yep.
没错。

751
00:38:56.320 --> 00:38:57.620
Angela's wearing jeans.
安吉拉穿了牛仔裤。

752
00:38:57.880 --> 00:38:58.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

753
00:38:58.680 --> 00:39:01.960
This is like, what, two times in the whole series she wore jeans?
这大概是整部剧里她第二次穿牛仔裤吧？

754
00:39:02.200 --> 00:39:02.720
Shocking.
太震惊了。

755
00:39:02.880 --> 00:39:03.280
Shocking.
太震惊了。

756
00:39:03.600 --> 00:39:09.000
And you can't really see, but I have on three and a half inch platform shoes.
而且你们可能看不出来，我穿了三英寸半的厚底鞋。

757
00:39:09.300 --> 00:39:09.940
You do?
真的吗？

758
00:39:10.220 --> 00:39:10.740
Sandals.
凉鞋。

759
00:39:11.100 --> 00:39:11.320
Yes.
是的。

760
00:39:11.580 --> 00:39:13.860
Because Angela has to run up and kiss Dwight.
因为安吉拉得跑过去亲德怀特。

761
00:39:14.140 --> 00:39:15.960
But Dwight is six foot three.
但德怀特身高六英尺三英寸。

762
00:39:16.440 --> 00:39:18.020
And Angela is five one.
而安吉拉只有五英尺一英寸。

763
00:39:18.300 --> 00:39:19.760
And I barely make it.
我几乎够不到他。

764
00:39:20.240 --> 00:39:20.600
Wow.
哇。

765
00:39:20.800 --> 00:39:22.760
I needed all the lift I could get.
我需要尽可能增加高度。

766
00:39:22.940 --> 00:39:24.920
So that was our sneaky way to give me some height.
所以这是我们偷偷让我变高的方法。

767
00:39:25.400 --> 00:39:27.660
Well, now Dwight is going to have a talking head.
好了，现在德怀特要进行单人访谈了。

768
00:39:27.660 --> 00:39:30.940
And he is taking us into the bullpen now, finally.
他终于带我们走进办公区了。

769
00:39:31.360 --> 00:39:35.740
And he explains he's hired some new faces and one old one.
他解释说他雇了一些新面孔，还有一张老面孔。

770
00:39:35.900 --> 00:39:38.680
And the person he's talking about is Devin.
他指的那个人就是德文。

771
00:39:39.060 --> 00:39:39.300
Yeah.
没错。

772
00:39:39.300 --> 00:39:41.200
We see Devin cross in the background.
我们看到德文从背景中走过。

773
00:39:41.620 --> 00:39:44.880
I love that we brought Devin back for this moment.
我很高兴我们能让德文回来参与这一刻。

774
00:39:45.580 --> 00:39:50.460
You guys remember Devin is the person that Michael fired in the first Halloween episode.
你们还记得德文就是迈克尔在第一季万圣节那集解雇的人吧。

775
00:39:50.460 --> 00:39:55.680
Both Creed and Devin were our stand-ins, starting with the pilot.
克里德和德文从试播集开始就是我们的替身演员。

776
00:39:55.980 --> 00:40:00.820
And the plot of the Halloween episode required that someone be fired.
万圣节那集的剧情需要有人被解雇。

777
00:40:01.080 --> 00:40:07.220
And it was between Creed or Devin, these two people, neither of whom had ever had lines.
当时要在克里德和德文之间选一个，这两个人之前都没有台词。

778
00:40:07.220 --> 00:40:13.100
And because Devin was leaving to do a play, Greg decided to fire Devin.
因为德文当时要离开去演舞台剧，格雷格决定解雇德文。

779
00:40:14.480 --> 00:40:15.760
But get this.
但你们听着。

780
00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:24.180
When they called Devin to ask him if he would come back for the finale, he was in New York doing another play.
当他们打电话问德文愿不愿意回来参加大结局时，他正在纽约演另一部舞台剧。

781
00:40:25.400 --> 00:40:27.820
It was like so full circle.
这简直是一个完美的轮回。

782
00:40:28.620 --> 00:40:30.800
But he was able to come back for it.
但他还是能回来参加。

783
00:40:30.900 --> 00:40:31.340
He was.
他是回来了。

784
00:40:31.480 --> 00:40:32.940
And here's something you guys should know.
还有件事你们应该知道。

785
00:40:33.080 --> 00:40:34.620
This was Creed's requeSt.
这是克里德的要求。

786
00:40:35.020 --> 00:40:41.800
We've talked about this before that Greg brought us all in to say, what is something you would want for your character as the show wraps up?
我们之前聊过，格雷格把我们都叫去问，在剧集结束时你们希望自己的角色有什么安排？

787
00:40:42.080 --> 00:40:45.120
And Creed said that he would love to see Devin come back.
克里德说他很想看到德文回来。

788
00:40:46.060 --> 00:40:47.520
I thought that was so sweet.
我觉得这太贴心了。

789
00:40:47.640 --> 00:40:48.400
So sweet.
太贴心了。

790
00:40:48.580 --> 00:40:49.320
And you know what?
而且你们知道吗？

791
00:40:49.420 --> 00:40:56.020
This is just one of the many little Easter eggs that's throughout the finale that are callbacks to the beginning of the show.
这只是大结局中众多小彩蛋之一，它们都是对剧集开头的呼应。

792
00:40:56.020 --> 00:40:57.380
I'm going to point out a few.
我会指出几个。

793
00:40:57.380 --> 00:41:01.120
And if you see any, let us know because I love finding them.
如果你们发现了什么，一定要告诉我们，因为我喜欢寻找这些彩蛋。

794
00:41:01.780 --> 00:41:05.900
Well, this is also when Creed is going to become himself.
嗯，这也是克里德即将展现真实自我的时候。

795
00:41:06.440 --> 00:41:07.000
Yes.
没错。

796
00:41:07.300 --> 00:41:14.660
It's going to be revealed that Creed is Creed Bratton from the band The Grassroots in the 60s, which is true.
剧情将揭示克里德就是60年代乐队“草根”的克里德·布拉顿，这是真的。

797
00:41:14.820 --> 00:41:17.480
Which is true, although the rest of it is not true.
这是真的，尽管其余部分都不是真的。

798
00:41:17.700 --> 00:41:17.820
Correct.
没错。

799
00:41:17.820 --> 00:41:23.240
He is not trafficking endangered species meat or has weapon-grade LSD.
他并没有非法贩卖濒危物种的肉，也没有武器级的LSD。

800
00:41:23.700 --> 00:41:24.140
Correct.
没错。

801
00:41:25.200 --> 00:41:26.920
But he is on the run now.
但他现在在逃亡中。

802
00:41:27.100 --> 00:41:31.520
The police are looking for him, and so that's why he left Dunder Mifflin, we learn.
我们得知警察正在搜捕他，这就是他离开邓德·米夫林的原因。

803
00:41:31.860 --> 00:41:32.080
Yeah.
没错。

804
00:41:32.540 --> 00:41:34.200
Big exodus from Dunder Mifflin.
邓德·米夫林迎来了一波大离职潮。

805
00:41:34.600 --> 00:41:35.280
Kevin's gone.
凯文走了。

806
00:41:35.440 --> 00:41:35.940
Now Toby.
现在是托比。

807
00:41:36.080 --> 00:41:36.700
Now Stanley.
现在是斯坦利。

808
00:41:37.240 --> 00:41:37.760
Creed.
克里德也是。

809
00:41:38.000 --> 00:41:38.300
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

810
00:41:39.280 --> 00:41:39.800
Daryl.
达里尔也是。

811
00:41:40.200 --> 00:41:40.620
Yeah.
没错。

812
00:41:41.280 --> 00:41:41.800
Nellie.
内莉也是。

813
00:41:42.140 --> 00:41:42.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

814
00:41:42.640 --> 00:41:43.960
Big, big changes.
非常、非常大的变动。

815
00:41:44.280 --> 00:41:44.460
Yeah.
是啊。

816
00:41:44.900 --> 00:41:47.560
Well, we're going to see that Phyllis has a new co-worker.
我们要看到菲利斯有了一位新同事。

817
00:41:48.060 --> 00:41:49.060
It's Malcolm.
是马尔科姆。

818
00:41:49.060 --> 00:41:51.980
And he loves her homemade fudge.
而且他很喜欢她做的自制软糖。

819
00:41:52.280 --> 00:42:01.220
Yes, she has a great talking head where she says, after 16 years, it's strange sitting across from somebody who isn't Stanley, but he'll get there.
是的，她有一个很棒的采访片段，她说十六年来第一次坐在一个不是斯坦利的人对面感觉很奇怪，但他会适应的。

820
00:42:01.680 --> 00:42:03.420
One piece of fudge at a time.
一次吃一块软糖慢慢适应。

821
00:42:05.560 --> 00:42:07.640
Well, Malcolm was played by Malcolm Barrett.
马尔科姆这个角色是由马尔科姆·巴雷特饰演的。

822
00:42:07.820 --> 00:42:15.920
I have known Malcolm for a long time because after The Office aired, I did a pilot with him called The 46 Percenters, and we played husband and wife.
我认识马尔科姆很久了，因为《办公室》播出后，我和他拍了一部试播集叫《46%的人》，我们在里面演夫妻。

823
00:42:16.080 --> 00:42:16.760
That's amazing.
太棒了。

824
00:42:17.040 --> 00:42:19.160
He went to NYU's Tisch School of the Arts.
他毕业于纽约大学帝势艺术学院。

825
00:42:19.180 --> 00:42:20.100
He's so talented.
他非常有才华。

826
00:42:20.260 --> 00:42:20.800
He's a playwright.
他是一位剧作家。

827
00:42:20.900 --> 00:42:21.440
He's an actor.
他也是位演员。

828
00:42:21.560 --> 00:42:22.160
He does it all.
他什么都能干。

829
00:42:22.160 --> 00:42:28.280
Yes, he's very well known for playing Rufus Carlin in Timeless, and he was also on Monk.
是的，他因在《穿越时间线》中饰演鲁弗斯·卡林而闻名，他也出演过《神探阿蒙》。

830
00:42:28.500 --> 00:42:29.720
Oh, Monk crossover.
哦，和《神探阿蒙》的联动。

831
00:42:30.260 --> 00:42:37.880
Well, I just love that you see him sitting in the background of Phyllis's talking head, and then you see him again in Jim's talking head,
我特别喜欢你在菲利斯的采访背景里看到他，然后在吉姆的采访里又看到了他，

832
00:42:37.880 --> 00:42:42.020
sitting there just like Leslie David Baker did for nine years.
就像莱斯利·大卫·贝克过去九年那样坐在那里。

833
00:42:42.180 --> 00:42:42.400
Yep.
没错。

834
00:42:42.800 --> 00:42:43.780
He's taken over.
他接替了那个位置。

835
00:42:43.780 --> 00:42:52.580
We also reveal another new face in the bullpen during Dwight's talking head, guest star alert, Dakota Johnson, who plays Dakota.
在德怀特的采访片段中，我们还揭晓了办公区里的另一张新面孔，客串明星预警，达科塔·约翰逊，她饰演达科塔。

836
00:42:53.000 --> 00:42:54.960
We're going to find out her name a little later on.
我们稍后会知道她的名字。

837
00:42:55.160 --> 00:42:58.400
You might know Dakota from the Fifty Shades of Grey movies.
你可能通过《五十度灰》系列电影认识达科塔。

838
00:42:58.800 --> 00:43:01.060
She's also the star of Madam Web.
她还是《蜘蛛夫人》的主演。

839
00:43:01.760 --> 00:43:10.180
Now, she originally had some scenes with the character of Clark, but they ended up being cut for time, so we don't see quite as much of her as was intended.
她原本和克拉克这个角色有一些对手戏，但最终因为时长原因被剪掉了，所以我们没能看到预想中那么多的戏份。

840
00:43:10.180 --> 00:43:14.340
You know, they do live on the deleted scenes on the DVD, and they're cute.
你知道，这些戏份被收录在DVD的删减片段里了，还挺可爱的。

841
00:43:14.520 --> 00:43:16.980
Clark and Dakota have this little flirty thing going.
克拉克和达科塔之间有点小暧昧。

842
00:43:17.320 --> 00:43:22.420
You can kind of see that they're like maybe the new next relationship if the show had kept going.
如果你仔细看，会发现如果剧集继续拍下去，他们可能就是下一对情侣。

843
00:43:22.620 --> 00:43:23.200
I see.
我明白了。

844
00:43:23.700 --> 00:43:27.740
Well, now we're going to move to the conference room, and we are going to find out some very big news.
现在我们要转到会议室，我们要得知一个非常重大的消息。

845
00:43:28.080 --> 00:43:36.080
Jim is sitting at the conference room table with a bunch of the other guys from the office and Dwight's cousin Zeke, played by Matt Jones.
吉姆正和办公室里的其他几个人，还有德怀特的表弟齐克（马特·琼斯饰）坐在会议桌旁。

846
00:43:36.080 --> 00:43:36.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

847
00:43:37.140 --> 00:43:41.960
Jim's going to tell us he has been made bestest mensch, best man.
吉姆要告诉我们他被选为“最佳伴郎”了。

848
00:43:42.380 --> 00:43:42.600
Yeah.
是啊。

849
00:43:42.860 --> 00:43:45.880
Well, I guess his party planning committee skills are going to come in handy.
我想他在派对筹备委员会练就的技能终于要派上用场了。

850
00:43:46.300 --> 00:43:49.220
Well, he doesn't have the best skills.
嗯，他的那些技能可算不上最好。

851
00:43:49.820 --> 00:43:51.280
He'll do better this time.
他这次会表现得更好。

852
00:43:51.400 --> 00:43:56.740
He's planned a night full of pranks, but all gutenpranks.
他计划了一整晚的恶作剧，但都是善意的恶作剧。

853
00:43:57.240 --> 00:43:57.640
Yes.
是的。

854
00:43:57.820 --> 00:44:02.680
He says after 12 years of tricking and pranking Dwight, tonight it's only going to be good surprises.
他说在捉弄了德怀特12年之后，今晚只会给他带来惊喜。

855
00:44:03.100 --> 00:44:03.720
Very sweet.
真贴心。

856
00:44:03.720 --> 00:44:07.160
The one person missing from this bachelor crew is Moe's.
这个单身派对小分队里唯一缺席的人是莫斯。

857
00:44:07.540 --> 00:44:10.060
Jim says to Dwight, are you sure Moe's isn't going to come?
吉姆问德怀特，你确定莫斯不会来吗？

858
00:44:10.200 --> 00:44:10.940
And Dwight's like, nope.
德怀特说，不来。

859
00:44:11.180 --> 00:44:13.460
He got weird ever since Angela moved in.
自从安吉拉搬进来后，他就变得很奇怪。

860
00:44:13.580 --> 00:44:17.920
He had to stop sleeping at the foot of my bed, and I don't know how he's feeling about this whole wedding thing.
他不得不停止睡在我的床脚，我不知道他对于这场婚礼到底是什么感觉。

861
00:44:18.160 --> 00:44:18.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

862
00:44:18.940 --> 00:44:20.680
Is this a callback to dinner party?
这是在致敬《晚宴》那一集吗？

863
00:44:21.120 --> 00:44:22.540
Sleeping at the end of the bed.
睡在床脚。

864
00:44:23.100 --> 00:44:24.680
Is it a little Easter egg?
这是一个小彩蛋吗？

865
00:44:25.100 --> 00:44:25.920
I wonder.
我也在想。

866
00:44:26.240 --> 00:44:26.420
Yeah.
是啊。

867
00:44:26.920 --> 00:44:27.640
Could be.
有可能是。

868
00:44:28.260 --> 00:44:28.880
All right.
好吧。

869
00:44:28.880 --> 00:44:33.740
Now we're going to go to the airport that was not really an airport.
现在我们要去那个其实并不是机场的机场了。

870
00:44:34.940 --> 00:44:35.480
What?
什么？

871
00:44:35.860 --> 00:44:36.140
Yeah.
是啊。

872
00:44:36.460 --> 00:44:37.660
Was it something else?
那是别的地方吗？

873
00:44:37.900 --> 00:44:39.080
It was a bus terminal.
那是个汽车总站。

874
00:44:39.280 --> 00:44:40.580
Do you have a location, Brachdaf?
你有具体的地点吗，布拉赫达夫？

875
00:44:40.700 --> 00:44:40.940
Yeah.
有的。

876
00:44:41.200 --> 00:44:46.060
We dressed a bus terminal to look like the Wilkes-Barre International Airport.
我们将一个汽车总站伪装成了威尔克斯-巴里国际机场。

877
00:44:46.580 --> 00:44:53.460
When you see Daryl walking out, and then you see Andy standing next to a taxi sign, we made all that signage.
当你看到达里尔走出来，然后看到安迪站在出租车标志旁边时，那些标志都是我们做的。

878
00:44:53.680 --> 00:44:56.900
We used the real logo from the Wilkes-Barre International Airport.
我们用了威尔克斯-巴里国际机场的真实标志。

879
00:44:57.280 --> 00:44:59.700
It's a little, like, green and white airplane.
就是一个小小的，绿白相间的飞机图案。

880
00:45:00.240 --> 00:45:00.540
Oh.
哦。

881
00:45:00.980 --> 00:45:02.760
I thought we did a really nice job.
我觉得我们做得真的很棒。

882
00:45:02.900 --> 00:45:03.480
I do, too.
我也这么觉得。

883
00:45:04.120 --> 00:45:06.420
Andy has a talking head here where he's like, you know what?
安迪在这里有个采访镜头，他说，你知道吗？

884
00:45:06.420 --> 00:45:07.480
Sure, I'll talk about it.
当然，我愿意谈谈这个。

885
00:45:07.540 --> 00:45:07.940
Why not?
为什么不呢？

886
00:45:07.940 --> 00:45:16.220
But his audition for America's next a cappella sensation went viral, and they made it into one of those auto-tune songs.
但他参加《全美下一位阿卡贝拉歌星》的试镜视频火了，他们把它做成了那种电音自动调音歌曲。

887
00:45:16.580 --> 00:45:18.580
Yeah, and he has a nickname now.
是的，他现在有个绰号。

888
00:45:18.740 --> 00:45:20.020
It's Baby Wawa.
叫“娃娃瓦瓦”。

889
00:45:20.260 --> 00:45:21.040
Baby Wawa.
娃娃瓦瓦。

890
00:45:21.280 --> 00:45:23.940
Even the late-night comedy guys had a field day with it.
连深夜脱口秀的主持人们都拿这个大做文章。

891
00:45:24.180 --> 00:45:28.440
And then we see a clip from Weekend Update at Saturday Night Live.
然后我们看到了《周六夜现场》里《周末更新》栏目的片段。

892
00:45:28.720 --> 00:45:31.100
Bill Hader is playing Baby Wawa.
比尔·哈德在扮演“娃娃瓦瓦”。

893
00:45:31.300 --> 00:45:33.240
We got a fan question from Karen T.
我们收到了来自北卡罗来纳州温斯顿-塞勒姆的凯伦·T的粉丝提问，她说，

894
00:45:33.420 --> 00:45:36.460
in Winston-Salem, North Carolina, who said,
我特别想知道，这个段子是赛斯·梅耶斯写的吗？

895
00:45:36.460 --> 00:45:39.620
I'm dying to know, did Seth Meyers write this bit?
我知道他还在那里的时候通常都是他写段子。

896
00:45:39.740 --> 00:45:42.360
I know he usually wrote the bits when he was still there.
不，凯伦，这是格雷格写的。

897
00:45:43.080 --> 00:45:44.800
No, Karen, Greg wrote this.
剧本里就是这么写的。

898
00:45:44.920 --> 00:45:46.060
It was in the script.
而且，你知道，格雷格曾在《周六夜现场》工作过。

899
00:45:46.380 --> 00:45:48.400
And, you know, Greg had worked at SNL.
他认识那些人。

900
00:45:48.680 --> 00:45:49.840
He knew all those guys.
他认识那些人。

901
00:45:50.700 --> 00:45:57.900
Steve Burgess thinks he probably reached out to Lorne Michaels, and then Seth Meyers and Bill Hader recorded it from the set, and they sent it on over to us.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯觉得他可能联系了洛恩·迈克尔斯，然后塞斯·梅耶斯和比尔·哈德在片场录制了这段内容，并把它发给了我们。

902
00:45:58.420 --> 00:45:59.220
So cool.
太酷了。

903
00:45:59.420 --> 00:46:03.740
So cool that Greg can just, like, pick up the phone and be like, hey, Lorne, can you just do me a quick little favor?
格雷格居然能直接拿起电话说，嘿，洛恩，能帮我个小忙吗，这太酷了。

904
00:46:03.860 --> 00:46:04.240
Okay, thanks.
好的，谢谢。

905
00:46:04.340 --> 00:46:04.460
Bye.
再见。

906
00:46:04.460 --> 00:46:05.920
You know, it's funny.
你知道吗，这很有趣。

907
00:46:06.160 --> 00:46:15.800
One time when I was on The Tonight Show with Jay Leno, after we finish doing our interviews, this is a thing they do, after the show is wrapped,
有一次我上杰·雷诺的《今夜秀》，采访结束后，这是他们惯例要做的一件事，节目收尾之后，

908
00:46:15.840 --> 00:46:22.080
you walk out with Jay and the other guests, and you make promos for, like, that episode.
你会和杰以及其他嘉宾一起走出来，为那期节目拍些宣传片。

909
00:46:22.080 --> 00:46:24.180
And you, like, wave and stuff like that.
然后你要挥手之类的。

910
00:46:24.240 --> 00:46:25.680
It's, like, part of the experience.
这算是体验的一部分吧。

911
00:46:26.280 --> 00:46:34.500
But one time before we did the promos, Jay did a little bit, and I can't remember what it was for, but it was, like, one of these.
但有一次在拍宣传片之前，杰做了一个小段子，我不记得是为了什么，但就像是这种类型的。

912
00:46:34.760 --> 00:46:39.140
They were like, Jay, you have to do that funny, fake thing, and we're going to put it in a movie.
他们当时说，杰，你得做那个搞笑的假动作，我们要把它放进电影里。

913
00:46:40.640 --> 00:46:45.460
And, like, you're making a joke about some character, and it's, like, it went viral.
就像是在拿某个角色开玩笑，结果它火了。

914
00:46:45.920 --> 00:46:47.820
So I, like, watched one of these happen.
所以我亲眼目睹了这种事情的发生。

915
00:46:48.040 --> 00:46:50.020
I bet those guys do stuff like that all the time.
我敢说那些家伙肯定经常做这种事。

916
00:46:50.620 --> 00:46:51.400
You know what?
你知道吗？

917
00:46:51.420 --> 00:46:57.600
I do have a lot of late-night talk show stories that I want to share on Office Lady 6.0.
我确实有很多关于深夜脱口秀的故事想在《办公室女士 6.0》里分享。

918
00:46:58.420 --> 00:47:00.120
I know some of them.
我知道其中一些。

919
00:47:00.920 --> 00:47:03.520
Some of them might belong on Burn It to the Ground.
有些可能更适合放在《彻底摧毁》里讲。

920
00:47:03.700 --> 00:47:04.260
I know.
我知道。

921
00:47:04.840 --> 00:47:05.340
Hmm.
嗯。

922
00:47:05.660 --> 00:47:06.540
Well, save it.
好吧，留着以后说吧。

923
00:47:06.620 --> 00:47:07.320
Save it.
留着吧。

924
00:47:07.780 --> 00:47:10.540
We're back in the bullpen now, and we're going to see Dakota.
我们现在回到办公区，去看看达科塔。

925
00:47:10.820 --> 00:47:17.080
She's walking from accounting over to Oscar's new office, which appears to be Daryl's old office.
她正从会计部走向奥斯卡的办公室，看起来那是达里尔以前的办公室。

926
00:47:17.280 --> 00:47:19.920
And you can overhear this funny bit of dialogue.
你可以听到这段有趣的对话。

927
00:47:20.140 --> 00:47:21.680
Oscar's on the phone, and he's saying,
奥斯卡正在打电话，他说，

928
00:47:21.860 --> 00:47:26.040
Years ago, the senator promised a left turn lane by the Arby's.
多年前，参议员承诺在阿比快餐店旁修一条左转车道。

929
00:47:26.040 --> 00:47:29.020
So I want to know where in the name of Horsey Sauce is it.
所以我想知道，看在“好滋味酱”的份上，那条车道到底在哪儿。

930
00:47:29.240 --> 00:47:29.760
Hmm.
嗯。

931
00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:33.920
I think he's doing some state senator election business.
我觉得他是在处理州参议员的竞选事务。

932
00:47:34.200 --> 00:47:35.820
I think it's his campaign headquarters.
我觉得那是他的竞选总部。

933
00:47:36.120 --> 00:47:39.680
Well, there's tons of campaign signs in this office.
这个办公室里有很多竞选标语。

934
00:47:39.940 --> 00:47:40.480
There are.
确实有。

935
00:47:40.840 --> 00:47:42.740
Here's a little breakdown of what you'll see inside.
这里简单介绍一下你在里面会看到什么。

936
00:47:42.860 --> 00:47:46.640
There is a nameplate that says Oscar Martinez, head accountant.
有一个名牌写着奥斯卡·马丁内斯，首席会计师。

937
00:47:46.880 --> 00:47:48.840
So he's got in this little office.
所以他搬进了这个小办公室。

938
00:47:49.040 --> 00:47:51.100
And Angela's no longer head accountant.
而安吉拉不再是首席会计师了。

939
00:47:51.440 --> 00:47:55.680
He also has a Yankees coffee mug with pins in it and some plants
他还有一个插着针的洋基队咖啡杯，还有一些植物

940
00:47:55.680 --> 00:47:56.500
and some artwork.
和一些艺术品。

941
00:47:57.000 --> 00:48:03.700
This makes you wonder, who took over Daryl's job as, like, head of the warehouse?
这让人不禁好奇，谁接替了达里尔担任仓库主管的工作呢？

942
00:48:03.700 --> 00:48:05.760
Are they back down in the warehouse?
他们回到仓库里了吗？

943
00:48:05.760 --> 00:48:07.720
We don't need them up in the bullpen anymore.
我们不再需要他们待在办公区了。

944
00:48:07.900 --> 00:48:08.580
We don't know.
我们不知道。

945
00:48:08.720 --> 00:48:12.520
We also know that there's now probably two empty seats over in accounting.
我们还知道会计部现在可能空出了两个座位。

946
00:48:13.120 --> 00:48:13.640
Two?
两个？

947
00:48:13.860 --> 00:48:14.380
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

948
00:48:15.320 --> 00:48:15.580
Hmm.
嗯。

949
00:48:15.800 --> 00:48:15.960
Hmm.
嗯。

950
00:48:16.380 --> 00:48:19.080
Well, this is the scene that reveals why Kevin was fired.
好吧，这一幕揭示了凯文被解雇的原因。

951
00:48:19.080 --> 00:48:19.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

952
00:48:19.740 --> 00:48:24.080
It's because he invented a number called Kalevin.
这是因为他发明了一个叫“卡列文”的数字。

953
00:48:24.840 --> 00:48:30.220
And it was a magic number that would sort of magically balance all accounts.
那是一个神奇的数字，能以某种魔法般的方式平衡所有账目。

954
00:48:30.500 --> 00:48:30.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

955
00:48:31.620 --> 00:48:33.760
Back at the airport, Nellie is arriving.
回到机场，奈莉到了。

956
00:48:34.000 --> 00:48:36.340
She says she lives in Poland now.
她说她现在住在波兰。

957
00:48:36.560 --> 00:48:39.980
And they flew her out for the weekend to do the reunion panel.
他们让她周末飞过来参加重聚座谈会。

958
00:48:40.660 --> 00:48:43.320
Interestingly enough, though, she is not on the panel.
但有趣的是，她并没有出现在座谈会上。

959
00:48:43.640 --> 00:48:44.340
She is not.
确实没有。

960
00:48:44.340 --> 00:48:48.560
Although I did find in the shooting draft that she answers a question on the panel.
虽然我在拍摄剧本里发现她确实在座谈会上回答了一个问题。

961
00:48:48.720 --> 00:48:49.920
Well, she's not there.
好吧，她不在那儿。

962
00:48:50.760 --> 00:48:51.920
I looked for her.
我找过她。

963
00:48:52.100 --> 00:48:52.880
Something happened.
出事了。

964
00:48:53.220 --> 00:48:53.380
Yeah.
是啊。

965
00:48:54.060 --> 00:48:59.560
Maybe this was part of Greg's writing of the finale as we went along.
也许这是格雷格在拍摄过程中边写大结局边调整的结果。

966
00:48:59.800 --> 00:49:00.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

967
00:49:00.300 --> 00:49:03.480
And maybe she was unavailable the day they actually did the panel.
也许他们真正拍摄座谈会那天她没空。

968
00:49:03.660 --> 00:49:04.720
That's very likely.
很有可能。

969
00:49:05.020 --> 00:49:06.760
Well, she's not on that stage.
总之，她没在那个台上。

970
00:49:06.900 --> 00:49:07.100
Nope.
没错。

971
00:49:08.260 --> 00:49:11.560
Now, Toby is going to see her at the airport.
现在，托比去机场见她。

972
00:49:11.560 --> 00:49:12.680
And he runs up.
他跑了过去。

973
00:49:12.800 --> 00:49:13.900
He's so excited.
他非常兴奋。

974
00:49:13.900 --> 00:49:14.820
He says hello.
他向她打招呼。

975
00:49:15.060 --> 00:49:16.160
She is not thrilled.
她却一点也不高兴。

976
00:49:16.400 --> 00:49:16.640
No.
没有。

977
00:49:16.720 --> 00:49:18.260
They have a very awkward exchange.
他们的交流非常尴尬。

978
00:49:18.600 --> 00:49:20.820
He asks her if she's still dating Piotr.
他问她是否还在和皮奥特交往。

979
00:49:21.220 --> 00:49:21.600
Yeah.
是啊。

980
00:49:21.880 --> 00:49:22.700
She says no.
她说没有。

981
00:49:22.860 --> 00:49:24.700
And I thought I unfriended you.
还说“我以为我把你删了”。

982
00:49:25.340 --> 00:49:25.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

983
00:49:26.440 --> 00:49:28.960
Toby then asks her if she would like to share a cab.
接着托比问她要不要一起拼车。

984
00:49:29.100 --> 00:49:29.800
She says no.
她说不。

985
00:49:30.100 --> 00:49:33.540
I would like to point out that Toby, Nellie, and Andy all had to take a cab.
我想指出的是，托比、奈莉和安迪当时都得打车。

986
00:49:34.080 --> 00:49:35.300
Daryl had a limo.
达里尔有辆豪华轿车。

987
00:49:35.300 --> 00:49:38.900
And in the shooting draft, it said that Daryl also had on a Rolex.
而且在拍摄剧本里，写着达里尔还戴着一块劳力士。

988
00:49:39.540 --> 00:49:45.300
So they really wanted to highlight the fact that he has made this big career successful move.
所以他们真的很想强调他已经在事业上取得了巨大的成功。

989
00:49:45.800 --> 00:49:46.100
Yeah.
是啊。

990
00:49:47.120 --> 00:49:51.560
Well, Toby has a talking head here where we're going to find out what he's been up to.
好吧，托比在这里有个采访镜头，我们要了解一下他的近况。

991
00:49:51.860 --> 00:49:55.520
He has moved to New York to write the great American novel.
他搬到了纽约，去写那部伟大的美国小说。

992
00:49:55.880 --> 00:50:03.300
He has six roommates, which he says are better than friends because they have to give you one month's notice before they leave.
他有六个室友，他说室友比朋友好，因为他们搬走前必须提前一个月通知你。

993
00:50:03.640 --> 00:50:04.760
Womp womp.
真扫兴。

994
00:50:05.020 --> 00:50:05.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

995
00:50:05.070 --> 00:50:06.420
Still sad Toby.
依然是那个可怜的托比。

996
00:50:10.100 --> 00:50:16.420
This next scene was really fun because we got Ed Helms and Craig Robinson back into the bullpen.
接下来这场戏真的很有趣，因为我们让艾德·赫尔姆斯和克雷格·罗宾逊回到了办公区。

997
00:50:17.160 --> 00:50:22.180
Andy arrives to the office and is greeted with, I guess, a lot of pity.
安迪来到办公室，迎接他的，我想，是满满的同情。

998
00:50:22.780 --> 00:50:26.200
I mean, Phyllis gives him the bear hug of all bear hugs.
我是说，菲利斯给了他一个超级大拥抱。

999
00:50:26.200 --> 00:50:36.160
I want you guys to know in the shooting draft, it said that Phyllis gives Andy a big hug and he is supposed to, and I quote, delicately work his way out of it.
我想让你们知道，在拍摄剧本里，写的是菲利斯给了安迪一个大拥抱，而他应该，引用原文，“小心翼翼地从拥抱中挣脱出来”。

1000
00:50:36.160 --> 00:50:38.660
But Phyllis doesn't stop hugging him.
但菲利斯一直没松手。

1001
00:50:38.920 --> 00:50:39.080
Aw.
噢。

1002
00:50:39.260 --> 00:50:40.980
This moment is in the bloopers.
这一幕在花絮里。

1003
00:50:41.180 --> 00:50:42.060
It is so funny.
太搞笑了。

1004
00:50:42.460 --> 00:50:43.440
Ed really lost it.
艾德真的笑场了。

1005
00:50:43.520 --> 00:50:44.180
You got to hear it.
你一定要听听。

1006
00:50:44.460 --> 00:50:45.340
How are you?
你好吗？

1007
00:50:45.840 --> 00:50:46.680
I'm good.
我很好。

1008
00:50:47.140 --> 00:50:48.040
Very good.
非常好。

1009
00:50:48.040 --> 00:50:50.780
A little, a little warm, actually.
其实有点，有点热。

1010
00:50:51.680 --> 00:50:52.380
Thank you.
谢谢。

1011
00:50:52.980 --> 00:50:53.920
Aw, thanks.
噢，谢谢。

1012
00:50:54.140 --> 00:50:54.560
Thank you.
谢谢。

1013
00:50:55.700 --> 00:50:56.740
Thank you, Phyllis.
谢谢你，菲利斯。

1014
00:51:11.250 --> 00:51:13.350
He could not get out of her hug.
他没法从她的拥抱里挣脱出来。

1015
00:51:13.490 --> 00:51:18.890
He was trying to delicately, like, weasel his way out of it and she had him in that hug.
他当时想委婉地，像黄鼠狼一样溜走，但她紧紧地抱住了他。

1016
00:51:18.890 --> 00:51:20.970
Like, he was like, I'm not going anywhere.
就像是，他当时心想，我哪儿也去不了了。

1017
00:51:21.250 --> 00:51:22.210
That was so funny.
那太搞笑了。

1018
00:51:23.470 --> 00:51:32.070
Now Daryl arrives and Dwight comes out of his office and he's so surprised to see these guys, he thought they couldn't come to the wedding.
现在达里尔到了，德怀特从办公室出来，看到这些人他非常惊讶，他以为他们没法参加婚礼。

1019
00:51:32.530 --> 00:51:33.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1020
00:51:33.350 --> 00:51:37.710
They clearly haven't factored them into their guest liSt.
他们显然没把这些人算进宾客名单里。

1021
00:51:37.970 --> 00:51:41.870
Lady, we got so much mail about this, about wedding etiquette.
女士，我们收到了很多关于这个的邮件，关于婚礼礼仪的。

1022
00:51:42.090 --> 00:51:42.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1023
00:51:42.350 --> 00:51:47.470
It was like people were saying, I do not understand this wedding guest liSt.
就像人们在说，我不理解这个婚礼宾客名单。

1024
00:51:47.470 --> 00:51:51.610
I do not understand how this wedding is going to absorb these surprise guests.
我不理解这场婚礼要怎么容纳这些不请自来的客人。

1025
00:51:52.130 --> 00:51:54.350
Angela must not be thrilled about this.
安吉拉肯定对此很不高兴。

1026
00:51:54.990 --> 00:51:55.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1027
00:51:55.390 --> 00:51:56.310
I thought about it, too.
我也想过这个问题。

1028
00:51:56.410 --> 00:51:57.990
I thought, okay, well, we know the wedding.
我想，好吧，我们知道这场婚礼的情况。

1029
00:51:58.090 --> 00:51:59.550
Everyone just sits on a hay bale.
大家只是坐在干草堆上。

1030
00:51:59.670 --> 00:52:01.810
So maybe they're not worried about the actual ceremony.
所以也许他们并不担心正式的仪式。

1031
00:52:01.950 --> 00:52:04.330
But what about the dinner at the reception?
但婚宴晚餐怎么办？

1032
00:52:04.810 --> 00:52:05.570
The food.
食物。

1033
00:52:05.690 --> 00:52:08.210
Do we have enough food for all these surprise people?
我们有足够的食物给这些不请自来的客人吗？

1034
00:52:09.110 --> 00:52:16.150
Well, Dwight is thrilled and it is revealed that they're really there for the panel, that the documentary crew paid to fly them in.
好吧，德怀特很兴奋，而且真相大白，他们其实是来参加座谈会的，是纪录片摄制组出钱让他们飞过来的。

1035
00:52:16.150 --> 00:52:20.790
And it was just sort of kismet that it was the same weekend as the wedding.
而且刚好和婚礼在同一个周末，真是天意。

1036
00:52:20.970 --> 00:52:22.510
So now they can go to both.
所以现在他们两边都能参加了。

1037
00:52:22.790 --> 00:52:24.570
Gemma's like, kismet my ass.
杰玛心想，天意个鬼。

1038
00:52:25.050 --> 00:52:30.710
I came up with excuses to make sure that these two things happened on the same weekend so that they could be here for the wedding.
我找了各种借口确保这两件事发生在同一个周末，这样他们就能来参加婚礼了。

1039
00:52:31.210 --> 00:52:32.290
Gutenpronk number one.
古滕普朗克第一条。

1040
00:52:32.650 --> 00:52:33.050
Exactly.
没错。

1041
00:52:33.050 --> 00:52:37.250
So now Pam enters and she is so excited to see Daryl.
现在帕姆进来了，她看到达里尔非常兴奋。

1042
00:52:37.470 --> 00:52:41.570
She wants to hear all about Austin and the Athlead merger.
她想听听关于奥斯汀和Athlead合并的所有事情。

1043
00:52:42.210 --> 00:52:44.330
Daryl says it's Athleap now.
达里尔说现在叫Athleap了。

1044
00:52:44.570 --> 00:52:45.470
Still lame.
还是很烂。

1045
00:52:45.910 --> 00:52:46.630
Still lame.
还是很烂。

1046
00:52:46.750 --> 00:52:47.630
It didn't get better.
没变好。

1047
00:52:47.750 --> 00:52:48.270
Didn't get better.
没变好。

1048
00:52:48.490 --> 00:52:49.050
Athleap?
Athleap？

1049
00:52:49.290 --> 00:52:51.370
I think Athleap is harder to say.
我觉得Athleap更难念。

1050
00:52:51.470 --> 00:52:52.150
I think it's worse.
我觉得更糟了。

1051
00:52:52.330 --> 00:52:53.210
I think it's worse.
我觉得更糟。

1052
00:52:54.130 --> 00:52:55.110
It's the P.
是那个P。

1053
00:52:55.630 --> 00:52:56.190
Athleap.
Athleap。

1054
00:52:56.690 --> 00:52:57.250
Athleap.
Athleap。

1055
00:52:57.690 --> 00:52:58.770
Athlead is better.
Athlead更好听。

1056
00:52:59.530 --> 00:53:00.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1057
00:53:01.030 --> 00:53:02.770
I need to point something out here.
我得指出一点。

1058
00:53:03.010 --> 00:53:10.430
At 5 minutes and 37 seconds, when Pam is entering this scene, she's kind of entering from that mystery hallway.
在5分37秒时，帕姆进入这个场景时，她是从那个神秘的走廊进来的。

1059
00:53:10.710 --> 00:53:12.670
The one behind the conference room.
就是会议室后面的那个。

1060
00:53:12.770 --> 00:53:15.690
The one where Dwight put firecrackers in the trash can.
德怀特往垃圾桶里放鞭炮的那个。

1061
00:53:15.850 --> 00:53:16.090
Yeah.
没错。

1062
00:53:16.210 --> 00:53:17.090
What is this place?
那到底是什么地方？

1063
00:53:17.290 --> 00:53:17.510
Okay.
好吧。

1064
00:53:17.510 --> 00:53:20.130
Well, it was scripted that I'm entering from the kitchen.
剧本里写的是我从厨房进来。

1065
00:53:20.790 --> 00:53:23.050
But for whatever reason, I don't.
但不知为何，我没那样做。

1066
00:53:23.130 --> 00:53:24.970
It was probably a camera angle thing.
可能跟摄像机角度有关。

1067
00:53:25.750 --> 00:53:27.450
And I'm watching this.
我正在看这一段。

1068
00:53:27.470 --> 00:53:28.390
And here we are.
现在我们看到这儿了。

1069
00:53:28.470 --> 00:53:29.950
It's the finale episode.
这是最后一集。

1070
00:53:30.590 --> 00:53:34.410
And I'm like, where does that hallway go?
我在想，那条走廊通向哪儿？

1071
00:53:34.570 --> 00:53:35.470
What is it?
那是什么？

1072
00:53:35.630 --> 00:53:36.810
We're at the finale.
我们都看到大结局了。

1073
00:53:36.810 --> 00:53:38.490
And I was on the show.
我还是剧里的演员。

1074
00:53:38.490 --> 00:53:41.290
And I still don't know what that is for.
但我到现在都不知道那是干嘛用的。

1075
00:53:41.490 --> 00:53:43.010
Not for purposes of the show.
在剧中没起过作用。

1076
00:53:43.210 --> 00:53:48.030
Now, in real life, we knew it was how you got to the stage from the hair and makeup tables.
现实生活中，我们知道那是从化妆间去舞台的通道。

1077
00:53:48.290 --> 00:53:48.550
Right.
对。

1078
00:53:48.790 --> 00:53:51.630
But it had no purpose in the world of the show.
但在剧里的世界观中，它毫无用处。

1079
00:53:51.950 --> 00:53:55.230
I sent Dave Rogers an email about it.
我为此给戴夫·罗杰斯发了封邮件。

1080
00:53:55.390 --> 00:53:58.550
I was like, Dave Rogers will tell me where this hallway goes.
我想，戴夫·罗杰斯肯定能告诉我那条走廊通向哪儿。

1081
00:53:58.630 --> 00:53:59.290
Yes, he will.
没错，他肯定知道。

1082
00:53:59.290 --> 00:54:02.210
He sent me a massive email.
他给我回了一封超长的邮件。

1083
00:54:02.490 --> 00:54:08.190
I mean, it was like, I don't even know how many pages long with charts and blueprints.
我是说，那邮件长得都不知道有多少页，还附带了图表和蓝图。

1084
00:54:08.290 --> 00:54:12.370
It was all about all of the hallways of Dunder Mifflin.
全是关于邓德·米夫林公司所有走廊的内容。

1085
00:54:12.370 --> 00:54:15.210
Honestly, it could be its own episode.
说实话，这都能单独拍一集了。

1086
00:54:15.590 --> 00:54:16.890
Here's what he said.
他是这么说的。

1087
00:54:17.030 --> 00:54:23.190
There is a deleted scene from Hot Girl that really explains a lot about these hallways.
在《辣妹》那一集里有个删减片段，对这些走廊做了很多解释。

1088
00:54:23.810 --> 00:54:26.310
I'm going to save it for Office Lady 6.0.
我要留到《办公室女士》6.0版本再说。

1089
00:54:26.630 --> 00:54:27.530
Oh, fantastic.
哦，太棒了。

1090
00:54:28.130 --> 00:54:29.690
But let me just say this.
但我只想说。

1091
00:54:30.210 --> 00:54:35.990
Even with Dave's dissertation on hallways, we may never know where this one went.
即便有了戴夫的走廊论文，我们可能永远也不知道那条走廊通向哪儿。

1092
00:54:37.250 --> 00:54:42.910
But I do want to do a full hallway breakdown on 6.0 because it's really amazing.
但我确实想在6.0版本里做一个完整的走廊解析，因为那真的很神奇。

1093
00:54:44.430 --> 00:54:45.270
I'm all in.
我完全赞成。

1094
00:54:45.390 --> 00:54:46.130
