所以老成员里有几个人在台上，但台下却空无一人。

1706
01:23:13.890 --> 01:23:14.630
No one's come.
一个人都没来。

1707
01:23:14.950 --> 01:23:16.350
And Andy says, I'm sorry.
安迪说，我很抱歉。

1708
01:23:16.350 --> 01:23:17.450
It's probably on me.
这可能都怪我。

1709
01:23:17.690 --> 01:23:20.150
I got a lot of hate when that auto tune went viral.
那段自动调音视频疯传时，我招来了很多谩骂。

1710
01:23:20.490 --> 01:23:21.330
He says, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1711
01:23:21.330 --> 01:23:22.410
I'll go talk to the manager.
我去跟经理谈谈。

1712
01:23:22.570 --> 01:23:24.150
Maybe we should just all go home.
也许我们应该直接回家了。

1713
01:23:24.450 --> 01:23:25.390
Just bail on this.
干脆放弃吧。

1714
01:23:25.390 --> 01:23:25.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1715
01:23:26.510 --> 01:23:32.250
Well, he walks out and there is a huge crowd of people waiting to load into the auditorium.
结果他走出去一看，外面有大批观众正等着进礼堂。

1716
01:23:32.430 --> 01:23:34.570
And they are so excited to see him.
他们都非常兴奋地想见到他。

1717
01:23:34.670 --> 01:23:39.870
They all start chanting, nard dog, and then clapping and saying, ra-da-da-da-da-doo.
他们开始高喊“纳德狗”，然后鼓掌并唱着“啦-哒-哒-哒-哒-嘟”。

1718
01:23:40.110 --> 01:23:41.390
It was so sweet.
那场面太温馨了。

1719
01:23:41.590 --> 01:23:50.670
The moment when Andy feels that love from them and he just can't wait and he says, ra-da-da-da-doo back.
安迪感受到他们的爱意，迫不及待地回应了“啦-哒-哒-哒-嘟”。

1720
01:23:50.670 --> 01:23:52.950
Ed played it so well.
艾德演得太棒了。

1721
01:23:53.090 --> 01:23:53.390
I know.
我知道。

1722
01:23:53.490 --> 01:23:54.110
I loved it.
我超喜欢。

1723
01:23:54.930 --> 01:23:57.670
The next scene is now a full auditorium.
下一个场景是座无虚席的礼堂。

1724
01:23:58.090 --> 01:24:02.690
Every seat is taken and all of the Dunder Mifflin employees are on stage.
每个座位都坐满了人，邓德·米夫林的员工们都在台上。

1725
01:24:02.970 --> 01:24:05.630
And there's a moderator taking questions from the crowd.
还有一位主持人正在接受观众提问。

1726
01:24:05.930 --> 01:24:09.070
I'd like to start with a list of the people who were on the panel.
我想先列出参加座谈会的人员名单。

1727
01:24:09.470 --> 01:24:09.610
Okay.
好的。

1728
01:24:09.610 --> 01:24:24.310
Clark, Aaron, Toby, Oscar, Meredith, Jim, Pam, Dwight, Daryl, Kevin, Andy, Phyllis, Pete, Stanley, and David Wallace.
克拉克、亚伦、托比、奥斯卡、梅雷迪思、吉姆、帕姆、德怀特、达里尔、凯文、安迪、菲利斯、皮特、斯坦利和大卫·华莱士。

1729
01:24:25.190 --> 01:24:27.430
Now I want to talk about who was not there.
现在我想谈谈谁没在场。

1730
01:24:28.430 --> 01:24:29.070
Creed.
克里德。

1731
01:24:29.470 --> 01:24:30.990
He was not on the panel.
他没参加座谈会。

1732
01:24:31.170 --> 01:24:32.310
But he was there.
但他确实在场。

1733
01:24:32.530 --> 01:24:33.890
He's in the audience.
他在观众席里。

1734
01:24:34.290 --> 01:24:34.510
He is.
没错。

1735
01:24:34.510 --> 01:24:35.650
He's shown at the very end.
他在最后露面了。

1736
01:24:36.570 --> 01:24:38.350
Here's who else was not there.
还有谁没在场呢？

1737
01:24:39.110 --> 01:24:39.550
Michael.
迈克尔。

1738
01:24:39.910 --> 01:24:42.810
The documentary crew did not fly in.
纪录片摄制组没有飞过来。

1739
01:24:43.130 --> 01:24:43.490
Michael.
迈克尔。

1740
01:24:43.850 --> 01:24:44.470
Surprising.
真令人惊讶。

1741
01:24:45.410 --> 01:24:48.310
Well, Greg and Steve did talk about this.
格雷格和史蒂夫确实讨论过这个问题。

1742
01:24:48.410 --> 01:24:53.750
Because as we all know, Michael Scott is going to surprise everyone at the wedding.
因为众所周知，迈克尔·斯科特会给婚礼上的每个人一个惊喜。

1743
01:24:53.930 --> 01:24:54.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1744
01:24:54.470 --> 01:25:02.170
And it was discussed, why would Michael come to the wedding and not come back, you know, and be the center of attention?
当时讨论过，迈克尔既然会来参加婚礼，为什么不回来成为焦点呢？

1745
01:25:02.170 --> 01:25:06.210
Wouldn't you think this isn't Michael Scott's personality to want to be on this panel?
你不觉得迈克尔·斯科特的性格根本不会想参加这种座谈会吗？

1746
01:25:06.210 --> 01:25:07.290
A hundred percent.
百分之百同意。

1747
01:25:07.290 --> 01:25:10.290
And we've established that it's happening the same weekend.
而且我们已经确定这发生在同一个周末。

1748
01:25:10.290 --> 01:25:12.330
So he is there in Scranton.
所以他当时就在斯克兰顿。

1749
01:25:12.470 --> 01:25:12.870
Yes.
是的。

1750
01:25:13.170 --> 01:25:19.510
Well, it was really important to Steve that we see growth from Michael Scott.
对史蒂夫来说，展现迈克尔·斯科特的成长真的很重要。

1751
01:25:19.510 --> 01:25:33.230
And he really believed in his heart that when Michael left and he married Holly and he started his new life, that he really lost this need for this kind of like public adoration.
他真心相信，当迈克尔离开、与霍莉结婚并开启新生活后，他确实不再需要那种公众的崇拜了。

1752
01:25:33.230 --> 01:25:39.390
You know, I can follow that because Michael, all he ever wanted was a family.
我明白，因为迈克尔一直以来想要的只是一个家庭。

1753
01:25:39.670 --> 01:25:39.930
Yes.
没错。

1754
01:25:40.050 --> 01:25:40.890
That's all he wanted.
他想要的仅此而已。

1755
01:25:41.010 --> 01:25:42.150
And he got his family.
而他最终也拥有了自己的家庭。

1756
01:25:42.290 --> 01:25:44.650
So he doesn't need this other thing anymore.
所以他不再需要那种东西了。

1757
01:25:44.930 --> 01:25:45.210
Yes.
是的。

1758
01:25:45.210 --> 01:25:48.150
And this is a departure from the British office.
这一点与英版《办公室》有所不同。

1759
01:25:48.710 --> 01:25:56.490
In the Christmas special for the British office, their documentary has aired and David Brent has become kind of a celebrity.
在英版《办公室》的圣诞特辑里，他们的纪录片已经播出，大卫·布伦特成了某种意义上的名人。

1760
01:25:56.830 --> 01:26:02.470
And so in that episode, he is just sort of reveling in his new fame.
在那一集中，他沉浸在自己新获得的声名中。

1761
01:26:02.650 --> 01:26:05.530
And I think there was also a desire to not repeat.
我想这也是为了避免重复。

1762
01:26:06.010 --> 01:26:06.550
Yeah.
没错。

1763
01:26:06.710 --> 01:26:10.790
And I also think that spot was already filled in our story with Andy.
而且我觉得在我们的故事里，那个位置已经被安迪填补了。

1764
01:26:11.150 --> 01:26:11.750
Exactly.
确实。

1765
01:26:12.750 --> 01:26:13.370
All right.
好吧。

1766
01:26:13.470 --> 01:26:15.090
Here's who else was not on the panel.
还有谁没参加座谈会呢？

1767
01:26:16.130 --> 01:26:17.510
Kelly and Ryan.
凯莉和瑞安。

1768
01:26:18.590 --> 01:26:20.190
They do show up at the wedding.
他们确实出现在了婚礼上。

1769
01:26:20.490 --> 01:26:20.830
They do.
没错。

1770
01:26:21.230 --> 01:26:27.470
Now, I 100% think that Kelly would want to be the center of attention on a panel.
我百分之百确定，凯莉肯定想成为座谈会的焦点。

1771
01:26:28.310 --> 01:26:30.870
Unfortunately, Mindy Kaling was not available this day.
遗憾的是，敏迪·卡灵那天没空。

1772
01:26:31.010 --> 01:26:32.870
And neither was BJ Novak.
B.J. 诺瓦克也没空。

1773
01:26:33.010 --> 01:26:35.010
So that's why they weren't on the panel.
所以他们才没参加座谈会。

1774
01:26:35.390 --> 01:26:38.450
We talked about Nellie, who shows up at the wedding.
我们聊到了奈莉，她出现在了婚礼上。

1775
01:26:38.650 --> 01:26:40.070
We don't know why she wasn't there.
我们不知道她为什么没参加座谈会。

1776
01:26:40.270 --> 01:26:41.070
Something happened.
肯定发生了什么事。

1777
01:26:41.070 --> 01:26:42.690
We have not gotten to the bottom of it.
我们还没查清楚原因。

1778
01:26:42.770 --> 01:26:44.410
I feel like it was a scheduling thing as well.
我觉得应该也是档期问题。

1779
01:26:44.690 --> 01:26:55.410
But here are some other people who I thought, if I'm tracking this as like the documentary bringing people back for fans to talk to, here's who I thought should have been there.
但还有一些人，如果我把这看作是纪录片把人们召集回来与粉丝交流，我觉得他们也应该在场。

1780
01:26:56.030 --> 01:26:56.550
Jan.
简。

1781
01:26:56.890 --> 01:26:57.950
For sure.
肯定的。

1782
01:26:58.530 --> 01:26:59.030
Roy.
罗伊。

1783
01:26:59.550 --> 01:27:00.030
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1784
01:27:00.490 --> 01:27:01.350
Todd Packer.
托德·帕克。

1785
01:27:01.490 --> 01:27:02.650
He would have loved it.
他肯定会乐在其中的。

1786
01:27:03.010 --> 01:27:03.390
Gabe.
盖博。

1787
01:27:05.330 --> 01:27:06.370
Robert California.
罗伯特·加利福尼亚。

1788
01:27:06.630 --> 01:27:07.670
Oh, that would have been delicious.
噢，那场面一定很精彩。

1789
01:27:08.170 --> 01:27:08.590
Karen.
凯伦。

1790
01:27:08.590 --> 01:27:09.410
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1791
01:27:10.190 --> 01:27:12.130
And there's one more person who's not there.
还有一个人没在场。

1792
01:27:12.370 --> 01:27:12.930
Oh, yeah.
噢，对。

1793
01:27:13.110 --> 01:27:14.150
It's you, Angela.
就是你，安吉拉。

1794
01:27:14.310 --> 01:27:14.770
I know.
我知道。

1795
01:27:15.150 --> 01:27:17.350
Do you want to share with everyone why you weren't there?
你想跟大家分享一下你为什么没在场吗？

1796
01:27:17.550 --> 01:27:21.250
I know Dwight says it's because you guys shouldn't see each other before the wedding.
我知道德怀特说是因为你们在婚礼前不该见面。

1797
01:27:21.390 --> 01:27:23.530
But there's a real reason why you weren't there.
但你没在场的真实原因是什么？

1798
01:27:23.710 --> 01:27:24.490
There is.
确实有原因。

1799
01:27:24.490 --> 01:27:26.090
So here's the deal.
事情是这样的。

1800
01:27:26.730 --> 01:27:32.170
As we started filming the finale, I was up for a really big role on a new sitcom.
当我们开始拍摄大结局时，我正在争取一部新情景喜剧里的重要角色。

1801
01:27:32.510 --> 01:27:35.330
It was a big deal for me because it was a lead.
这对我来说意义重大，因为那是个主角。

1802
01:27:35.590 --> 01:27:40.350
The show was called The Gabriels, and it would have been me and Rob Riggle playing husband and wife.
那部剧叫《加布里埃尔一家》，本来应该由我和罗伯·里格尔饰演夫妻。

1803
01:27:41.190 --> 01:27:42.590
Tim Meadows was in it.
蒂姆·梅多斯也参演了。

1804
01:27:42.590 --> 01:27:43.970
It was really great.
真的很棒。

1805
01:27:44.090 --> 01:27:45.130
The cast was phenomenal.
演员阵容非常强大。

1806
01:27:45.990 --> 01:27:51.610
And, you know, it's just one of those things that happens in life when everything you want to do all happens at the same time.
你知道，这就是生活中常有的事，你想做的一切刚好都在同一时间发生了。

1807
01:27:51.790 --> 01:27:52.110
Yes.
是的。

1808
01:27:52.490 --> 01:27:56.210
So they were both going to overlap the finale in this new pilot.
所以这两部戏的拍摄档期和这部新试播集的结尾撞上了。

1809
01:27:56.210 --> 01:27:59.910
I didn't know what to do, and I went to Greg, and I said, Greg, what should I do?
我不知道该怎么办，于是我去找格雷格，问他我该怎么做。

1810
01:28:00.310 --> 01:28:07.090
And, you know, Jenna, he was so kind, and he said, listen, I want this opportunity to happen for you, but I honestly don't know how to make it work.
你知道吗，珍娜，他非常体贴，他说，听着，我希望你能抓住这个机会，但我真的不知道该怎么协调。

1811
01:28:07.090 --> 01:28:13.210
He said if Steve Burgess could work his scheduling magic and figure it out, I had his blessing.
他说如果史蒂夫·伯吉斯能施展他的排期魔法搞定这件事，他会全力支持。

1812
01:28:13.890 --> 01:28:21.750
And creatively, he said he could take me out of this panel, that he could make it make sense for him, for the show, Why Angela Wouldn't Be There.
在创作层面，他说他可以把我从那场座谈会中剔除，他能让剧情安排合理，让安吉拉缺席变得合情合理。

1813
01:28:21.870 --> 01:28:22.110
Sure.
当然。

1814
01:28:22.250 --> 01:28:23.650
It's the morning of her wedding.
那天正好是她婚礼的早晨。

1815
01:28:23.650 --> 01:28:27.250
He could make that creatively make sense, and that would give me an extra day.
他能让这个情节在创作上说得通，这样我就能多出一天时间。

1816
01:28:27.690 --> 01:28:33.590
But then Steve Burgess rolled up his sleeve, and, you know, he's always been such a champion for us.
但后来史蒂夫·伯吉斯卷起袖子开始干活了，你知道，他一直是我们坚定的支持者。

1817
01:28:33.590 --> 01:28:41.350
And he knew, Jenna, that me playing the lead in something would mean I would get considered for bigger roles after The Office wrapped.
而且他知道，珍娜，如果我能出演主角，意味着《办公室》结束后，我会有机会获得更好的角色。

1818
01:28:42.130 --> 01:28:44.570
And I just love this man so much.
我真的太爱这个人了。

1819
01:28:44.670 --> 01:28:46.890
He got on the phone with the producers at Fox.
他给福克斯的制片人打了电话。

1820
01:28:47.090 --> 01:28:48.690
They worked it all out.
他们把一切都协调好了。

1821
01:28:49.350 --> 01:28:52.130
It included some crazy scheduling.
这涉及了一些疯狂的排期。

1822
01:28:52.130 --> 01:28:55.330
I had to film part of the Fox pilot on a Saturday.
我必须在周六拍摄部分福克斯的试播集。

1823
01:28:55.610 --> 01:28:57.930
On one day, I worked on both shows.
有一天，我同时在两部剧组工作。

1824
01:28:58.430 --> 01:29:03.030
Steve Burgess sent a van to pick me up on The Fox lot with the office hair and makeup team.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯派了一辆面包车到福克斯片场接我，车上带着《办公室》的妆发团队。

1825
01:29:03.030 --> 01:29:08.050
And they transformed me into Angela Martin driving down the freeway.
他们在高速公路上开车时，就把我变回了安吉拉·马丁的造型。

1826
01:29:08.390 --> 01:29:08.910
Amazing.
太神奇了。

1827
01:29:09.270 --> 01:29:13.050
I asked Steve what he remembered about all of this, and this is what he had to say.
我问史蒂夫他还记得这件事吗，他是这么说的。

1828
01:29:13.250 --> 01:29:19.310
One of my favorite things was talking with Kim Ferry about how she had to redo your hair on the drive to the set.
我最喜欢的回忆之一就是和金·费里谈论她如何在去片场的路上重新为你做造型。

1829
01:29:19.590 --> 01:29:21.690
Kim and I still laugh and talk about that.
我和金至今还会谈起这件事并大笑。

1830
01:29:21.930 --> 01:29:23.510
But that was just part of it.
但这只是其中一部分。

1831
01:29:23.650 --> 01:29:25.850
I spoke with the pilot people all the time.
我一直在和试播集那边的人沟通。

1832
01:29:25.850 --> 01:29:30.190
We worked out a schedule that we thought would work but unfortunately might actually kill you.
我们制定了一个我们认为可行，但遗憾的是可能会把你累垮的排期。

1833
01:29:30.390 --> 01:29:31.690
But you survived.
但你挺过来了。

1834
01:29:31.690 --> 01:29:34.470
Both schedules had to change a lot during the shooting.
拍摄期间，两个剧组的排期都变动了很多次。

1835
01:29:34.650 --> 01:29:35.370
We ran long.
我们拍摄超时了。

1836
01:29:35.530 --> 01:29:36.770
They had to reschedule stuff.
他们不得不重新安排很多事情。

1837
01:29:36.910 --> 01:29:38.150
But it all worked out.
但最终一切都解决了。

1838
01:29:38.310 --> 01:29:42.950
You were amazing shooting two shows, both demanding, and you came through looking great.
你同时拍摄两部要求极高的剧集，表现得太棒了，而且看起来状态还那么好。

1839
01:29:43.270 --> 01:29:47.230
Well, I remember that day that you arrived to set and you had gotten ready in the van.
嗯，我记得你那天到达片场时，已经在车里做好了造型。

1840
01:29:48.170 --> 01:29:49.930
It was so crazy.
真是太疯狂了。

1841
01:29:51.090 --> 01:29:58.090
You know, when I watch these scenes, I do get a little emotional because, oh, obviously for so many reasons,
你知道，当我看到这些场景时，我确实有点感触，因为，显而易见，原因有很多，

1842
01:29:58.270 --> 01:30:05.250
but also because Greg and Steve did that for me because they knew it would help my career after the office.
但也是因为格雷格和史蒂夫为我做了这些，因为他们知道这对我《办公室》之后的职业生涯有帮助。

1843
01:30:05.450 --> 01:30:06.670
And that was such a gift.
那真是一份大礼。

1844
01:30:06.670 --> 01:30:11.610
And I did find something really special to me in my digital clutter about it.
我在我的数字杂物里找到了一些关于这件事的特别的东西。

1845
01:30:12.490 --> 01:30:18.870
I sent two people an email about my new look on the Gabriels, my fancy hair.
我给两个人发了邮件，说了我在《加布里埃尔一家》里的新造型，我那华丽的发型。

1846
01:30:19.130 --> 01:30:21.850
I emailed you and my dad.
我发给了你和我爸爸。

1847
01:30:22.230 --> 01:30:27.010
I sent you both a picture and I said, this is my new look for the Gabriels.
我给你们俩都发了照片，说，这是我在《加布里埃尔一家》里的新造型。

1848
01:30:27.210 --> 01:30:30.550
You wrote back, lady, you look amazing!
你回信说，亲爱的，你看起来太棒了！

1849
01:30:30.910 --> 01:30:32.130
Two exclamation points.
用了两个感叹号。

1850
01:30:32.130 --> 01:30:38.070
And my dad wrote, Ange, I like it, LOL, which he thought meant lots of love.
我爸爸回信说，安吉，我很喜欢，LOL，他以为那是“满满的爱”（Lots of Love）的意思。

1851
01:30:38.190 --> 01:30:38.450
Yes.
是的。

1852
01:30:38.670 --> 01:30:39.290
Bill Kinsey.
比尔·金西。

1853
01:30:40.150 --> 01:30:40.490
Hmm.
嗯。

1854
01:30:41.550 --> 01:30:42.730
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

1855
01:30:43.850 --> 01:30:47.530
Well, it was a little bittersweet for me, Angela, that you weren't there.
嗯，安吉拉，你没能到场，这对我来说有点苦乐参半。

1856
01:30:47.770 --> 01:30:52.170
This was my second favorite scene that we shot for the finale.
这是我们在大结局中拍摄的第二喜欢的场景。

1857
01:30:52.450 --> 01:30:54.090
You said it was really moving.
你说过这真的很感人。

1858
01:30:54.690 --> 01:30:55.930
It really was.
确实如此。

1859
01:30:55.930 --> 01:31:04.110
It was special because Greg filled this scene with so much of our crew and our office family.
这很特别，因为格雷格在这个场景里安排了我们很多剧组成员和办公室大家庭的成员。

1860
01:31:04.790 --> 01:31:07.990
You know, Greg created a type of yearbook for us.
你知道，格雷格为我们制作了一本类似毕业纪念册的东西。

1861
01:31:08.090 --> 01:31:13.870
And when I was rewatching the finale, and in particular this scene, I saw all those familiar faces.
当我重看大结局，特别是这一幕时，我看到了所有那些熟悉的面孔。

1862
01:31:13.870 --> 01:31:19.930
And I was so grateful to him that we have these people on camera.
我非常感激他，让我们能把这些人拍进镜头里。

1863
01:31:20.790 --> 01:31:24.530
So he made our writers and other crew members.
他让我们的编剧和其他剧组成员参与进来。

1864
01:31:25.390 --> 01:31:28.090
He gave them roles asking the questions.
他给了他们提问的角色。

1865
01:31:28.510 --> 01:31:35.090
And he said it really worked because if someone was a little stiff or maybe not the best actor,
他说这效果很好，因为如果有人表现得有点僵硬，或者演技不是最好的，

1866
01:31:35.090 --> 01:31:39.030
it's like, well, that's what a real person in the audience would be like.
那就好比，嗯，现实中的观众大概就是那个样子。

1867
01:31:39.210 --> 01:31:43.630
Well, you know, I think we should do a breakdown as well of the special guests that are in this scene.
嗯，你知道，我觉得我们也应该分析一下出现在这个场景里的特别嘉宾。

1868
01:31:43.750 --> 01:31:44.890
Yes, let's talk about it.
好的，我们来聊聊这个。

1869
01:31:45.150 --> 01:31:47.730
The moderator is played by Suzanne Daniels.
主持人是由苏珊·丹尼尔斯扮演的。

1870
01:31:47.950 --> 01:31:48.890
Greg's wife.
格雷格的妻子。

1871
01:31:49.210 --> 01:31:51.170
I thought she did a fantastic job.
我觉得她表现得太棒了。

1872
01:31:51.170 --> 01:31:54.570
The first question was asked by Brent Forrester.
第一个问题是布伦特·福雷斯特问的。

1873
01:31:55.530 --> 01:31:58.390
Amelie Gillette asked about Jim giving up athlete.
阿梅莉·吉列特问了关于吉姆放弃运动员生涯的问题。

1874
01:31:59.050 --> 01:32:03.550
Writer Allison Silverman said Jim could do anything, and I mean anything.
编剧艾莉森·西尔弗曼说吉姆什么都能做，我是说真的什么都能做。

1875
01:32:03.830 --> 01:32:04.630
She was so funny.
她太搞笑了。

1876
01:32:04.710 --> 01:32:05.550
So funny.
太搞笑了。

1877
01:32:05.850 --> 01:32:09.910
